Regular.ttf\nNotoSansCoptic-Regular.ttf\nNotoSansCuneiform-Regular.ttf\nNotoSansCypriot-Regular.ttf\nNotoSansInscriptionalPahlavi-Regular.ttf\nNotoSansInscriptionalParthian-Regular.ttf\nNotoSansMiao-Regular.otf\nNotoSansOldPermic-Regular.otf\nNotoSansTamil-VF.ttf\n/system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc\n/system/fonts/NotoSerifCJK-Regular.ttc\nTTF\n\n\nFont: /system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc index 2 = SC. Let me verify index and also check bold variant availability. NotoSansCJK has weight variants as separate files usually. Let me check if there's a Bold ttcollection.\n\nActually there might be /system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Bold.ttc. Let me check. Also check what index 0/1/2 are.\n\nLet me now design the full production.\n\nPlan:\n- 1920x1080, 60fps\n- Duration ~72s\n- Story with protagonist 小陈\n\nScenes with narration. Let me write narration lines (Chinese), generate each with edge-tts, measure duration, then compute scene start times.\n\nNarration script (9 segments):\n\nS1 (开场, ~8s): "凌晨两点，小陈打开电脑，准备提交他的毕业设计。可当他登录 GitHub，屏幕上出现了一行他从未见过的提示。"\nS2 (~7s): "您的账号已被停用。三年积累的仓库、星标、贡献记录，全部变成灰色。"\nS3 (~9s): "他慌了。第一反应是注册小号，换个网络，再给官方连发十几封邮件。这些动作，恰恰会让情况更糟。"\nS4 (~9s): "冷静下来之后，他学到第一件事：GitHub 的封禁分两种，一种是机器误判，一种是真实违规。"\nS5 (~8s): "他核对了自己的记录，没有任何违规行为，属于典型的垃圾信息检测误报。这一类，是可以申诉的。"\nS6 (~9s): "第二件事，找到正确的入口。打开 support.github.com，选择账号停用申诉，填上用户名、邮箱和理由。"\nS7 (~11s): "第三件事，写一封说清事实的申诉信。不要情绪，不要哀求，只写三件事：我是谁，我没有违规，请人工复核。"\nS8 (~9s): "提交之后，把工单号记下来。一到三个工作日内等待回复，不要重复开单，也不要频繁更换登录环境。"\nS9 (~9s): "第三天，一封来自 GitHub Support 的邮件到了：检测系统误判，账号已恢复。"\nS10 (~8s): "申诉不是求情，而是证明那台机器判错了。"\n\nTotal ~87s of narration. Plus gaps → ~92s. That's fine (>60s).\n\nHmm, that might be long to render at 1080p60. 92s * 60fps = 5520 frames at 1920x1080. PIL rendering... each frame maybe 30-60ms → 5520 * 0.05 = 276s ≈ 4.6 min. Plus piping to ffmpeg. Acceptable but let's be careful. Actually with numpy-heavy drawing could be slower. Let's estimate: previous 960 frames at 1280x720 took "one to two minutes" per my earlier claim. 5520 frames at 1080p is 5.75x pixels... could be 10-15 min. Hmm.\n\nMaybe reduce: target ~70-75s total. Trim narration a bit.\n\nLet me be efficient: use numpy for background gradients (precompute per scene), and draw with PIL. Precompute expensive static layers once per scene, then per-frame only animate overlays.\n\nStrategy for performance:\n- For each scene, precompute a base image (background gradient + light blobs composited) once.\n- Per frame: copy base, draw animated elements (particles, text with reveal progress, progress bar), convert to bytes.\n\nCopy of 1920x1080 RGB image is fast (~6MB memcpy). Drawing text per frame is the cost. Text reveal animations with per-line alpha require re-drawing text each frame. That's maybe 20-40 text draws per frame → could be slow-ish but PIL text draw is fast (~1ms each) → 40ms/frame. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: reduce per-frame text redraw by rendering text layers with cached sprites and compositing with alpha. Better: for each scene, pre-render each text line as a separate RGBA sprite once (with full opacity). Then per frame, paste with computed alpha offset via Image.alpha_composite or paste with mask scaled. Pasting RGBA sprite with varying alpha requires creating an alpha-adjusted copy — that's a numpy operation on small sprite, fast.\n\nSimpler and fast enough: pre-render full scene text composite at a few progress steps? That reduces smoothness.\n\nLet me do: per-line sprite caching. Each line sprite ~ (width x 80). Adjusting alpha: use numpy on sprite alpha channel: arr[:,:,3] = (a*alpha).astype(uint8). Small array → fast.\n\nThen paste onto frame with offset for slide-in.\n\nParticles: draw small circles with alpha — use a precomputed particle sprite and alpha adjust, or just draw with ImageDraw on RGBA overlay then composite. 30 particles → fine.\n\nMotion graphics ideas (动画):\n- Animated background: gradient + moving light blobs (precompute blobs as alpha sprites, paste at animated positions)\n- Particles drifting up\n- Text: line-by-line fade + slide up\n- Scene transitions: cross fade\n- Story-specific visuals:\n  - S1: laptop screen glow, night window, clock ticking 02:00\n  - S2: login screen mock with "Account suspended" banner sliding in, red\n  - S3: three wrong moves — icons with red X, shaking\n  - S4: two paths branching (green/red)\n  - S5: checklist ticking off with check marks\n  - S6: browser mock form filling animation (cursor typing)\n  - S7: letter/email composing with lines appearing\n  - S8: timeline/progress with waiting spinner\n  - S9: email inbox notification pop\n  - S10: closing with summary\n\nThat's a lot of custom drawing. I need to be pragmatic but deliver real quality.\n\nI'll build a frame renderer with scene-specific draw functions. Let me design a consistent visual system:\n- Deep navy gradient bg (#0B1220 → #131C2E)\n- Accent colors: green #3FB950, red #F85149, blue #58A6FF, amber #F0B429\n- Card panels: rounded rect with subtle border\n- Font: CJK regular + bold (use stroke_width for bold effect)\n\nLet me check bold font file first.\n\nAlso need to handle: PIL text with stroke.\n\nLet me plan the code architecture:\n\n```python\nW,H = 1920,1080\nFPS = 60\n\nscenes = [ {id, dur, narration_text, draw_fn} ]\n```\n\nFirst generate narration audio, get durations, compute timeline.\n\nTimeline: scene_dur = audio_dur + 0.6 gap (min 5.0)\n\nThen render frames.\n\nThen audio mix: voiceover concatenated at scene starts (each segment starts at scene_start + 0.3), BGM at low volume with ducking (sidechaincompress or just static low volume).\n\nAlso add subtle whoosh/notification SFX? Could add simple synthesized effects: typing clicks, notification ding, success chime. That adds production value. Let me synthesize with numpy: \n- notification ding (sine 880 + 1320 with decay)\n- success chime (arpeggio)\n- error thud\nKeep it simple but present.\n\nAudio mixing plan:\n1. voice.mp3 -> wav 48k stereo, placed at offsets\n2. bgm.wav synthesized (longer, ~duration) at -22dB with ducking\n3. sfx placed at specific times\n\nThen amix/concat. Use ffmpeg-amix with adelay.\n\nSimpler: do mixing in Python with numpy at 48kHz, write final WAV, then mux with video. That gives full control. Yes — do audio entirely in numpy.\n\nLet me now write steps:\n\nStep 1: check bold font.\nStep 2: write narration script + generate audio, get durations (edge-tts, 10 segments).\nStep 3: write render script.\nStep 4: render + encode.\nStep 5: audio mix + mux.\nStep 6: verify.\nStep 7: cleanup + screen off/on.\n\nLet me check bold font and voice options.\n\nFor voice: use zh-CN-YunxiNeural (male, warm) for narration, and maybe zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural for 小陈's inner thoughts? Two voices adds production value. Also could use zh-CN-YunjianNeural (male, sports/news). Let's use YunxiNeural for narration and XiaoxiaoNeural for GitHub email readout in S9.\n\nActually for the email content in S9, reading it with a different voice (female, official tone) would be nice: "检测系统误判（spam detecting systems highlight accounts that need to be manually reviewed），账号已恢复，仓库和 gist 已重新可用。"\n\nGood.\n\nLet me check bold fonts available.🔧 调用工具: batch_command\n参数: {"commands": ["ls /system/fonts/ \p grep -iE 'CJK\pHan\pMipro\pRoboto-(Bold\pRegular)' \p head", "python3 -c \\"from PIL import ImageFont; f=ImageFont.truetype('/system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc',40,index=2); print(f.getname()); print('CJK ok')\\"", "python3 -c \\"from PIL import ImageFont;\\nimport sys\\nfor i in range(8):\\n try:\\n  f=ImageFont.truetype('/system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc',40,index=i); print(i, f.getname())\\n except Exception as e: print(i,'ERR'); break\\""], "timeout": 40}\n结果: 批量执行 3 条命令：\nNotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc\nNotoSansHanifiRohingya-Regular.otf\nNotoSansHanunoo-Regular.ttf\nNotoSerifCJK-Regular.ttc\nRoboto-Regular.ttf\nSysSans-Hans-Regular.ttf\nSysSans-Hant-Regular.ttf\n('Noto Sans CJK SC', 'Regular')\nCJK ok\n0 ('Noto Sans CJK JP', 'Regular')\n1 ('Noto Sans CJK KR', 'Regular')\n2 ('Noto Sans CJK SC', 'Regular')\n3 ('Noto Sans CJK TC', 'Regular')\n4 ('Noto Sans CJK HK', 'Regular')\n5 ('Noto Sans Mono CJK JP', 'Regular')\n6 ('Noto Sans Mono CJK KR', 'Regular')\n7 ('Noto Sans Mono CJK SC', 'Regular')\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 -c \\"\\nimport asyncio, edge_tts\\nasync def m():\\n    vs = await edge_tts.list_voices()\\n    zh = [v['ShortName'] for v in vs if v['Locale'].startswith('zh-CN')]\\n    print(zh)\\nasyncio.run(m())\\n\\" 2>&1 \p tail -3", "timeout": 60}\n结果: ['zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural', 'zh-CN-XiaoyiNeural', 'zh-CN-YunjianNeural', 'zh-CN-YunxiNeural', 'zh-CN-YunxiaNeural', 'zh-CN-YunyangNeural', 'zh-CN-liaoning-XiaobeiNeural', 'zh-CN-shaanxi-XiaoniNeural']\n\n\nFont confirmed: /system/fonts/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc index 2 = SC. No bold CJK; I'll use stroke_width for bold, or NotoSerifCJK for contrast (Serif for headings could look premium). Actually mixing Serif for titles and Sans for body is a nice design choice.\n\nVoices: YunxiNeural (male warm), YunyangNeural (male professional news), XiaoxiaoNeural (female), XiaoyiNeural (female young), YunjianNeural (male sports).\n\nPlan: narration = YunxiNeural (warm male storytelling), email readout = YunyangNeural (official/professional male).\n\nNow let me write the narration script and generate audio. I'll create a python file that generates all audio segments.\n\nLet me write the story script carefully with 10 scenes.\n\nScene list with narration (aim ~75-85s total video):\n\n1. **[夜] 开场** (~7s)\n   "凌晨两点，小陈准备提交他的毕业设计。登录 GitHub 的那一刻，屏幕上弹出了一行他从未见过的提示。"\n   \n2. **[封禁] 发现被封** (~7s)\n   "您的账号已被停用。三年的仓库、星标、还有那一片绿色的贡献格子，一瞬间全部变灰。"\n   \n3. **[慌乱] 错误反应** (~9s)\n   "他慌了。第一反应是注册小号、切换网络、再连发十几封邮件。这三个动作，恰恰会让情况变得更糟。"\n   \n4. **[冷静] 分类** (~9s)\n   "冷静下来之后，他查到了第一件事：GitHub 的封禁分两种。一种来自自动风控的误判，一种来自真实违规。"\n   \n5. **[核查] 自查** (~8s)\n   "他逐条核对了自己的操作记录，没有刷量，没有侵权，没有批量注册。这是典型的垃圾信息检测误报。"\n   \n6. **[入口] 找对地方** (~9s)\n   "第二件事，找对入口。打开 support.github.com，选择账号停用申诉，填上用户名、绑定邮箱和申诉理由。"\n   \n7. **[话术] 写申诉信** (~11s)\n   "第三件事，写一封只讲事实的申诉信。不要哀求，不要指责，只写三句：我是谁，我没有违规，请人工复核。"\n   \n8. **[等待] 跟进** (~8s)\n   "提交之后记下工单号，等待一到三个工作日。不要重复开单，那只会让排队重新开始。"\n   \n9. **[解封] 收到回信** (~9s)\n   "第三天，邮件到了。'检测系统误判，需要人工复核。账号已重置，仓库和 gist 已恢复。'"\n   \n10. **[收尾] 总结** (~7s)\n    "申诉不是求情，而是证明那台自动判定的机器，这次真的判错了。"\n\nTotal narration ≈ 83s + gaps 10*0.6 = 6s → ~89s. That's a good length (>60s).\n\nHmm, 89s * 60fps = 5340 frames at 1920x1080. Rendering time concern. Let me optimize:\n\nOptimization plan:\n- Precompute per-scene static base (gradient + vignette) once\n- Cache text line sprites\n- Use numpy for compositing\n- Write frames via pipe to ffmpeg rawvideo\n\nLet me estimate: per frame operations:\n1. base.copy() → 6.2MB copy ≈ 3ms\n2. N sprite pastes with alpha → each on small region, maybe 0.5ms each\n3. particles 30 draws\nTotal maybe 15-25ms/frame → 5340 frames ≈ 110-220s. Plus PNG/pipe encode. OK, ~3-5 min. Acceptable.\n\nFor encoding: pipe raw RGB to ffmpeg -f rawvideo. That's 6.2MB per frame → 5340*6.2MB = 33GB through pipe. That's a lot of I/O but local pipe, maybe ok at ~500MB/s → 66s. Fine.\n\nLet's do it.\n\nDesign details per scene — I'll write a drawing framework:\n\n```python\nclass Canvas:\n    def __init__(self, w, h): self.img = Image.new('RGB',(w,h))\n```\n\nElements:\n- `bg_base(scene_idx, t)`: precomputed gradient + animated blobs\n- Text lines with `reveal` progress\n- Cards\n\nLet me define a consistent layout:\n- Title at top-left with section number\n- Content area\n- Bottom progress bar\n- Watermark / chapter label\n\nLet me write actual code. I need to be careful about code correctness since I can't see the frames. I'll validate with OCR and pixel statistics.\n\nKey lesson from before: the Draw object must bind to the correct image. I'll be careful.\n\nLet me write the script in parts.\n\nI'll create ~/vt/gen.py with:\n\n1. Scenes definition: id, kind, dur (computed from audio), narration, subs (list of text lines with style), and a scene-specific visual function.\n\n2. Rendering loop.\n\n3. Audio generation: edge-tts for narration, numpy for BGM + SFX, mix into final wav.\n\n4. Encode via ffmpeg pipe.\n\nLet me be systematic. First, generate the narration audio and get exact durations — that determines the timeline.\n\nWrite ~/vt/tts.py:\n\n```python\nimport asyncio, edge_tts, json, subprocess, os\n\nLINES = [\n ("s1", "zh-CN-YunxiNeural", "凌晨两点，小陈准备提交他的毕业设计。登录 GitHub 的那一刻，屏幕上弹出了一行他从未见过的提示。"),\n ...\n]\n```\n\nGenerate each to mp3, then ffprobe duration.\n\nThen compute timeline. Then render.\n\nLet me write and run tts.py now.\n\nAlso: I should add rate/pitch variations for expressiveness. edge-tts supports rate="+10%" etc. Narration slightly slower: rate="-5%" maybe for clarity. Let's use default for narration, and for the panicked scene S3 use rate="+12%" pitch="+8Hz" to convey urgency. Nice touch.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nAlso for S9 email readout use zh-CN-YunyangNeural with rate="-8%" official tone.\n\nLet me define:\ns1: Yunxi, "凌晨两点，小陈准备提交他的毕业设计。登录 GitHub 的那一刻，屏幕上弹出了一行他从未见过的提示。"\ns2: Yunxi, "-20%" ... hmm actually slower for gravity: rate="-10%" "您的账号，已被停用。三年的仓库、星标，还有那一整片绿色的贡献格子，一瞬间全部变灰。"\ns3: Yunxi rate="+15%" "他慌了。第一反应是注册小号、切换网络、再连发十几封邮件。可这三个动作，恰恰会让情况变得更糟。"\ns4: Yunxi "冷静下来之后，他查到了第一件事。GitHub 的封禁，分两种：一种来自自动风控的误判，一种来自真实违规。"\ns5: Yunxi "他逐条核对了自己的操作记录。没有刷量，没有侵权，没有批量注册。这是典型的垃圾信息检测误报。"\ns6: Yunxi "第二件事，找对入口。打开 support 点 github 点 com，选择账号停用申诉，填上用户名、绑定邮箱，和申诉理由。"\n  - Careful with URL pronunciation: write "support.github.com" → TTS might read oddly. Better to write "support 点 github 点 com" as text? For TTS the text "support.github.com" might be read as "support github com" which is fine.\n  Let me write: "打开 support.github.com，选择账号停用申诉，填上用户名、绑定邮箱，和申诉理由。"\ns7: Yunxi rate="-5%" "第三件事，写一封只讲事实的申诉信。不要哀求，不要指责。只写三句话：我是谁，我没有违规，请人工复核。"\ns8: Yunxi "提交之后，记下工单号，等待一到三个工作日。不要重复开单，那只会让你的排队重新开始。"\ns9: Yunyang rate="-5%" "第三天，邮件到了。检测系统出现了误判，账号已重置，仓库和 gist 已经恢复。"\ns10: Yunxi rate="-8%" "申诉，不是求情。而是证明那台自动判定的机器，这一次，真的判错了。"\n\nGood. ~10 scenes.\n\nNow visual design per scene. Let me think about what's drawable and looks premium:\n\nCommon elements:\n- Background: vertical gradient #070B14 → #101A2B, plus 2-3 large radial "glow" blobs in blue/teal that slowly drift, plus a subtle grid, plus vignette.\n- Particles: 40 small dots drifting up with varying alpha.\n- Top-left: chapter chip like "01 / 10" + section title\n- Bottom: thin progress bar with glowing head\n- Scene transitions: 0.5s crossfade\n\nScene-specific visuals:\n\nS1 夜/笔记本: Draw a stylized laptop in the center: screen rectangle glowing, keyboard base trapezoid, on screen a tiny code editor mock with colored lines. Behind, a window with moon + city silhouette. Clock text "02:00" top-right blinking.\n- Animation: screen glow pulsing, cursor blinking in code, city lights twinkling.\n\nS2 封禁: A browser window mock center with GitHub-like header, then a big red banner slides down: "Your account has been suspended". Below, small text. Repos list items fade to gray one by one.\n- Animation: banner slide + shake, items desaturate sequentially.\n\nS3 慌乱: Three wrong-action cards appear in sequence with red X marks: "注册小号", "切换网络", "狂发邮件". Screen edges flash red, slight shake.\n- Animation: cards pop in with elastic, red pulse ring.\n\nS4 分类: Two paths branching from a node — left green "风控误判" with label 可申诉, right red "真实违规". Lines draw progressively.\n- Animation: path draw-on, then cards fade in.\n\nS5 核查: A checklist panel with 4 items and checkmarks drawing on one by one; then a verdict stamp "SPAM 误报" appearing.\n\nS6 入口: Browser mock with URL bar typing "support.github.com", then a form with fields filling.\n\nS7 话术: An email compose panel; three lines of text appearing with typing animation; plus a side note "不要哀求 / 不要指责".\n\nS8 等待: A timeline with day markers, a progress line growing, spinner turning, "1-3 工作日" text.\n\nS9 解封: An email inbox card with a notification icon popping, sender "GitHub Support", subject line, and quoted body text; green success glow; account status flipping from Suspended (red) to Active (green).\n\nS10 收尾: Summary lines + big statement. Fade to end card.\n\nThis is a lot of drawing code, but doable. Let me write it carefully with helper functions:\n\nHelpers:\n- rr(draw, box, radius, fill, outline, width) — rounded rect\n- text_c(draw, xy, s, font, fill, anchor) \n- glow_circle\n- card panel with shadow\n\nI'll build with PIL ImageDraw on RGB image, using a separate RGBA overlay for glows maybe.\n\nTo keep it manageable, I'll implement a single `draw_scene(i, t_local, t_scene)` function with if/elif per scene id.\n\nText reveal: I'll implement `fade_slide(img, sprite, x, y, alpha, dy)`.\n\nSprite cache: `make_text_sprite(text, font, color, stroke)` returns RGBA image.\n\nFor alpha adjust with cache: store the sprite, and each frame do:\n```\nif alpha >= 0.99: img.paste(sprite, (x,y), sprite)\nelse: \n    a = sprite.getchannel('A').point(lambda v: int(v*alpha))\n    img.paste(sprite, (x,y), a)\n```\npoint() on small image is fast enough.\n\nOK. Also need Chinese text rendering with proper font. Bold: use stroke_width=2 + stroke_fill=same color to fake bold, or use NotoSerifCJK for titles.\n\nLet me use:\n- TITLE font: NotoSerifCJK-Regular.ttc index 2 (SC serif) at various sizes — looks premium\n- BODY font: NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc index 2\n\nCheck NotoSerifCJK indices — probably same order (JP,KR,SC,TC,HK...). I'll test.\n\nLet me now write the audio generation first, get durations, then the renderer.\n\nI'll write files with create_file.\n\nOne concern: total runtime of the tool call. Rendering may take several minutes. I should use run_background for the render and poll. That's safer.\n\nPlan:\n1. Write tts.py, run it → get durations JSON.\n2. Write render.py with timeline from JSON.\n3. Run render in background with log, poll.\n4. Mix audio + mux.\n5. Verify.\n6. Cleanup.\n\nLet me write tts.py now.\n\nAlso test NotoSerifCJK index quickly in same call.\n\nLet me go.🔧 调用工具: create_file\n参数: {"path": "/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/tts.py", "content": "# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\nimport asyncio, json, os, subprocess\\nimport edge_tts\\n\\nBASE = \\"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt\\"\\nAUD = os.path.join(BASE, \\"aud\\")\\nos.makedirs(AUD, exist_ok=True)\\n\\n# (id, voice, rate, pitch, text)\\nLINES = [\\n    (\\"s01\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+0%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"凌晨两点，小陈准备提交他的毕业设计。登录 GitHub 的那一刻，屏幕上弹出了一行他从未见过的提示。\\"),\\n    (\\"s02\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"-12%\\", \\"-2Hz\\",\\n     \\"您的账号，已被停用。三年的仓库、星标，还有那一整片绿色的贡献格子，一瞬间全部变灰。\\"),\\n    (\\"s03\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+18%\\", \\"+6Hz\\",\\n     \\"他慌了。第一反应是注册小号、切换网络，再连发十几封邮件。可这三个动作，恰恰会让情况变得更糟。\\"),\\n    (\\"s04\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+0%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"冷静下来之后，他查到了第一件事。GitHub 的封禁分两种：一种来自自动风控的误判，一种来自真实违规。\\"),\\n    (\\"s05\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+0%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"他逐条核对了自己的操作记录。没有刷量，没有侵权，没有批量注册。这是典型的垃圾信息检测误报。\\"),\\n    (\\"s06\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+0%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"第二件事，找对入口。打开 support.github.com，选择账号停用申诉，填上用户名、绑定邮箱，和申诉理由。\\"),\\n    (\\"s07\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"-6%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"第三件事，写一封只讲事实的申诉信。不要哀求，不要指责。只写三句话：我是谁，我没有违规，请人工复核。\\"),\\n    (\\"s08\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"+0%\\",  \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"提交之后，记下工单号，等待一到三个工作日。不要重复开单，那只会让你的排队重新开始。\\"),\\n    (\\"s09\\", \\"zh-CN-YunyangNeural\\", \\"-6%\\", \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"第三天，邮件到了。检测系统出现了误判，账号已重置，仓库和 gist 已经恢复。\\"),\\n    (\\"s10\\", \\"zh-CN-YunxiNeural\\", \\"-10%\\", \\"+0Hz\\",\\n     \\"申诉，不是求情。而是证明那台自动判定的机器，这一次，真的判错了。\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef dur(p):\\n    r = subprocess.run([\\n        \\"ffprobe\\", \\"-v\\", \\"error\\", \\"-show_entries\\", \\"format=duration\\",\\n        \\"-of\\", \\"csv=p=0\\", p], capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    try:\\n        return float(r.stdout.strip())\\n    except Exception:\\n        return 0.0\\n\\n\\nasync def main():\\n    out = []\\n    for sid, voice, rate, pitch, text in LINES:\\n        p = os.path.join(AUD, sid + \\".mp3\\")\\n        for attempt in range(4):\\n            try:\\n                c = edge_tts.Communicate(text, voice, rate=rate, pitch=pitch)\\n                await c.save(p)\\n                if os.path.getsize(p) > 2000:\\n                    break\\n            except Exception as e:\\n                print(\\"retry\\", sid, attempt, e, flush=True)\\n                await asyncio.sleep(1.5)\\n        d = dur(p)\\n        out.append({\\"id\\": sid, \\"voice\\": voice, \\"text\\": text,\\n                    \\"dur\\": round(d, 3), \\"path\\": p})\\n        print(sid, round(d, 3), flush=True)\\n\\n    with open(os.path.join(BASE, \\"timing.json\\"), \\"w\\", encoding=\\"utf-8\\") as f:\\n        json.dump(out, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)\\n    total = sum(x[\\"dur\\"] for x in out)\\n    print(\\"TOTAL_NARRATION\\", round(total, 2), flush=True)\\n\\n\\nasyncio.run(main())\\n"}\n结果: ✅ 创建 /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/tts.py (3283 字节)\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "python3 -c \\"\\nfrom PIL import ImageFont\\nfor i in range(6):\\n    try:\\n        f=ImageFont.truetype('/system/fonts/NotoSerifCJK-Regular.ttc',40,index=i); print(i,f.getname())\\n    except Exception as e: print(i,'ERR'); break\\n\\"", "timeout": 30}\n结果: 0 ('Noto Serif CJK JP', 'Regular')\n1 ('Noto Serif CJK KR', 'Regular')\n2 ('Noto Serif CJK SC', 'Regular')\n3 ('Noto Serif CJK TC', 'Regular')\n4 ERR\n\n\nSerif SC index 2 confirmed. Now run tts.py.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 tts.py 2>&1 \p tail -20", "timeout": 300}\n结果: s01 9.264\ns02 10.68\ns03 8.856\ns04 9.264\ns05 10.008\ns06 10.488\ns07 12.168\ns08 9.336\ns09 8.136\ns10 9.72\nTOTAL_NARRATION 97.92\n\n\nTotal narration 97.92s. Plus gaps → ~102s video. That's 6120 frames at 1080p60. That's a lot but manageable (>60s requirement satisfied).\n\nHmm, that's long. Maybe fine — user wants 60s+. 100s is good.\n\nLet me reduce slightly? No, 97.92s narration + 10 scenes * ~0.7s gaps = ~105s. 105*60 = 6300 frames.\n\nRendering estimate: if 25ms/frame → 158s ≈ 2.6min. Plus pipe I/O. OK.\n\nBut I need robustness. Let me render in background with progress logging.\n\nNow let me carefully design the renderer.\n\nStructure:\n\n```python\nW,H = 1920,1080\nFPS = 60\nSCENE_GAP = 0.75  # silence before next scene starts\nLEAD_IN = 1.2     # before first narration\nTAIL = 2.5\n\ntimeline:\n  t = LEAD_IN\n  for each scene: start = t; dur = audio_dur + GAP; t += dur\n  total = t + TAIL\n```\n\nActually a scene's visual duration should be audio_dur + GAP, and narration starts at scene_start + 0.25.\n\nCrossfade between scenes: 0.5s.\n\nRendering approach: for each scene, render frames from scene_start to scene_end, with local time. For crossfade, blend with previous scene's last frame — that requires rendering prev scene frame too. Simpler: instead of crossfade between scenes, use "fade from black" for the first and fade-to-black at end, plus per-scene fade-in of elements (which reads as smooth transitions). Also I can do a quick "dip" effect: fade to a dark tint at scene boundaries (last 0.3s of scene fade out, first 0.3s fade in). That's cheap: multiply frame brightness by a factor. Good — visually reads smooth without needing crossfade buffers.\n\nActually a crossfade would look better but cost is double render. Dip-to-dark is acceptable and clean.\n\nI'll do: global brightness = f(t) where f dips at scene boundaries. Implement via numpy multiply on frame at boundaries only (fast).\n\nLet me now design the visual language in code.\n\nCommon:\n- BG: precompute per scene a base 1920x1080 RGB:\n  - vertical gradient from (8,12,20) to (18,26,42)\n  - a large radial glow (blue #1f4b7a) at animated position — but animation needs per-frame. I'll precompute a few glow sprites and paste with alpha each frame (cheap).\n  - subtle grid lines (precomputed in base)\n  - vignette (precomputed in base)\n\