 from 985 to 1355 — extends left of the box (1120) and overlaps rows region. That's a layout bug!\n\nI intended center at 1350. Let me fix: blit at (1350, 806).\n\nLet me check sprite width: 判定：SPAM 误报 → 判定(2*46) + ：(46) + SPAM(4*~28) + spaces + 误报(2*46) ≈ 92+46+112+2*46 = 342. Half=171. So currently spans 999..1341, inside box 1120..1580 partially. So text is left-shifted out of box.\n\nFix: center at 1350.\n\nAlso let me double check other anchor usages for similar mistakes:\n- s05 rows fine.\n- s10 text centered at W//2 with anchor ct → good.\n- s03 caption W//2 anchor cm → good.\n- s01 subtitle panel 560-1370, text at 640 anchor lm → good.\n- s02 translation 960 cm → good.\n- s06 title etc fine.\n- s07 bottom text 960 cm → good.\n- s09 "Suspended" at 1420 lm in chip 1380-1740 → good.\n\nSo just fix stamp center x to 1350.\n\nAdditionally, to make the stamp look like a stamp, keep rotation.\n\nLet me patch and re-test at t=50.\n\nAlso verify scene 6/7 typing and scene 9 status flip at later time (e.g., 95 for scene 9 with Restored). Already saw 96 shows "Restored". Good.\n\nLet me patch.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\np='render.py'\\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\\ns=s.replace('        blit(img, 1170, 806, s, sp, anchor=\\"cm\\", rot=4)',\\n            '        blit(img, 1350, 806, s, sp, anchor=\\"cm\\", rot=4)')\\ns=s.replace('        d.rounded_rectangle([1120, 762, 1580, 852], radius=10,',\\n            '        d.rounded_rectangle([1180, 762, 1520, 852], radius=10,')\\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('ok')\\nPYEOF\\npython3 render.py --test 50 2>&1 \p tail -3\\npython3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nImage.open('/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/test/f_050.0.png').convert('RGB').crop((1130,745,1570,870)).resize((880,250), Image.LANCZOS).save('/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/test/stamp2.png')\\nEOF\\ntesseract ~/vt/test/stamp2.png - -l chi_sim+eng --psm 11 2>/dev/null \p tr -s '\\\\n ' ' '", "timeout": 300}\n结果: ok\nTOTAL 109.520s  FRAMES 6571\nsaved 50.0\n. \n\nStill OCR empty. Let me check whether the stamp text is actually being rendered at all. Let me isolate: render only the stamp by measuring green pixel bounding box in the crop region excluding the rectangle outline.\n\nBetter: let me directly test the sprite creation and blit in isolation.\n\nActually, a likely bug: in `blit`, when `rot` is given, `s.rotate(..., expand=True)` is called — fine. But then `s.getchannel("A")` on rotated RGBA works.\n\nHmm. But wait: `sprite(...)` returns cached sprite; then `.resize()` creates a new image. Fine.\n\nLet me check if the issue is that `sp` at t=50 → lt = 50-42.464 = 7.536; stamp sp = clamp01((7.536-4.2)/0.5) = 1.0. So should be fully drawn.\n\nLet me measure green pixels in region excluding outline: crop inside (1200,770)-(1500,845).\n\nLet me do a quick isolated test.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\\nimport numpy as np, importlib.util\\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\"r\\",\\"render.py\\")\\nr=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(r)\\n# 单独测试 sprite\\ns=r.sprite(\\"判定：SPAM 误报\\",\\"serif\\",46,r.C_GRN,True)\\nprint(\\"sprite size\\", s.size)\\na=np.asarray(s)\\nprint(\\"非透明像素\\", int((a[:,:,3]>10).sum()))\\ns.save('test/only_stamp.png')\\n# 再看 f_050 内部区域绿像素\\nim=Image.open('test/f_050.0.png').convert('RGB')\\nc=np.asarray(im.crop((1200,772,1500,842))).astype(int)\\nprint(\\"内部区域 绿亮像素\\", int((c[:,:,1]>90).sum()))\\nEOF", "timeout": 120}\n结果: sprite size (387, 60)\n非透明像素 9288\n内部区域 绿亮像素 6462\n\n\nSprite is fine (387x60, 9288 px). And the frame's inner region has 6462 green bright pixels → the text IS drawn at the right place.\n\nSo OCR just can't read green-on-dark small text well. Fine — the stamp is there. Let me OCR the isolated sprite to confirm text correctness.\n\nActually let me OCR test/only_stamp.png.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && tesseract test/only_stamp.png - -l chi_sim+eng --psm 7 2>/dev/null; python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nimport numpy as np\\ns=Image.open('/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/test/only_stamp.png').convert('RGBA')\\nbg=Image.new('RGBA',(s.width+40,s.height+40),(255,255,255,255))\\nbg.alpha_composite(s,(20,20))\\nbg.convert('L').save('/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/test/stamp_white.png')\\nprint(\\"ok\\")\\nEOF\\ntesseract ~/vt/test/stamp_white.png - -l chi_sim+eng --psm 7 2>/dev/null", "timeout": 120}\n结果: 判定: SPAM 误报\nok\n判定: SPAM 误报\n\n\nThe stamp text is correct: "判定: SPAM 误报" (OCR reads ：as :). \n\nNow everything verified. Time for full render. 6571 frames at 1920x1080. Let me estimate time: render a 60-frame burst and time it.\n\nLet me test speed: render frames quickly with a timing test.\n\nActually just run in background and monitor. But first quick timing check to know if it'll take too long.\n\nLet me time 100 frames via a small script that renders without encoding.\n\nActually simplest: run the full render in background and poll the log. If too slow I can adjust (e.g., preset ultrafast).\n\nLet me do a quick timing test first.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport time, importlib.util\\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\"r\\",\\"render.py\\")\\nr=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(r)\\ntl,total=r.load_timeline()\\nt0=time.time()\\nfor i in range(60):\\n    r.render_frame(i/60.0, tl)\\nd=time.time()-t0\\nprint(\\"60帧耗时 %.2fs → 单帧 %.1fms\\"%(d, d/60*1000))\\nprint(\\"全片预估 %.1f 分钟\\"%(6571*d/60/60))\\nEOF", "timeout": 300}\n结果: 60帧耗时 2.24s → 单帧 37.3ms\n全片预估 4.1 分钟\n\n\n37ms/frame → 4.1 min for video render. Encoding adds time but ffmpeg runs in parallel with pipe. Let's run in background.\n\nMeanwhile, prepare the audio: BGM synthesis + mixing.\n\nLet me write audio.py while video renders.\n\nActually let me start the render in background first, then write audio.\n\nNote: rendering opens a pipe to ffmpeg; background run with log file.\n\nLet me start it.🔧 调用工具: run_background\n参数: {"command": "cd /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt && python3 render.py > render.log 2>&1", "log_file": "/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/render.log"}\n结果: ✅ 后台 PID: 10881\n日志: /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/render.log\n\nNow write audio.py while rendering.\n\nAudio design:\n- Sample rate 48000\n- Total duration from plan.json (109.52s)\n- Load narration mp3s → decode to wav 48k mono via ffmpeg → numpy\n- Place at scene.start + 0.25 offset\n- BGM synthesized with musical arc\n- SFX\n- Ducking under voice\n- Normalize, write stereo wav\n\nBGM synthesis details:\n\nTempo: 92 BPM → beat = 60/92 = 0.652s. Bar (4/4) = 2.609s.\n\nChord progression with emotional arc:\nSections:\n- 0-22.9 (S1,S2): Am - Fmaj7 (sparse pad, low)\n- 22.9-42.4 (S3,S4): Dm - Am - E (tension, pulse)\n- 42.4-64.4 (S5,S6): Cmaj7 - G/B - Am - F (hopeful, arpeggio + perc)\n- 64.4-87.3 (S7,S8): Fmaj7 - G - Em - Am (build)\n- 87.3-109.5 (S9,S10): C - G - Am - F, then final C resolve, fade\n\nSimplify: define chord list per bar index with a function chord_for_bar(bar).\n\nInstruments:\n1. pad(freqs, dur): sum of detuned saws with lowpass via simple one-pole filter, slow attack.\n2. piano(freq, dur): additive harmonics with exponential decay.\n3. bass(freq, dur): sine + slight odd harmonics, punchy attack.\n4. bell(freq, dur): FM with fast decay.\n5. kick(t): sine sweep 120→45 with fast decay + click.\n6. hat(t): filtered noise short.\n7. snare: noise + tone.\n\nReverb: simple multi-tap delay with feedback and lowpass.\n\nI'll implement with numpy, mono then stereo widening (slight delay on right).\n\nLet me write it carefully but compactly.\n\nFrequencies: use MIDI note to freq: f = 440 * 2**((n-69)/12)\n\nChord definitions (MIDI notes):\nAm: root A2=45, notes [57,60,64] (A3,C4,E4)\nFmaj7: F2=41, notes [53,57,60,64]\nDm: D3=50, [57,62,65]\nE: E2=40, [56,59,64]\nCmaj7: C3=48, [55,59,64,71] → simplify [48,55,59,64]\nG: G2=43, [55,59,62]\nEm: E3=52, [55,59,64]\nC: C3=48, [52,55,60]\n\nLet me define progression as list of (bar, chord) over the whole duration and just tile.\n\nBar length = 2.6087s → total bars = 109.52/2.6087 ≈ 42 bars.\n\nProgression plan by bar:\nbars 0-2 (0-7.8s): Am pad only\nbars 3-6 (7.8-18.3): Am, Fmaj7, Am, Fmaj7 (add low pulse)\nbars 7-9: Dm, Am, E\nbars 10-13: Dm, E, Am, Fmaj7\nbars 14-17: C, G, Am, F\nbars 18-21: C, G, Am, F (arpeggio + perc)\nbars 22-25: F, G, Em, Am\nbars 26-29: F, G, Em, Am\nbars 30-33: C, G, Am, F (full)\nbars 34-37: C, G, Am, F\nbars 38-40: F, G, C\nbars 41: C (final, fade)\n\nThat's 42 bars. Good.\n\nLayers by time:\n- pad: full time (volume envelope)\n- bass: from bar 3 to bar 40\n- piano arpeggio: from bar 10\n- bell melody: bars 18-37\n- kick: bars 14-37 (soft), and bars 30-37 stronger\n- hat: bars 18-37\n- snare: bars 30-37 every 2 beats\n\nVolume arc: 0.35 → 0.6 → 0.55 → 0.4 → 0 (fade)\n\nThen duck under narration using voice envelope.\n\nSFX:\n- error thud at scene2 start + 0.35 (banner appears)\n- keyboard clicks during scene 6 typing (0.5-2.0) and scene 7 typing\n- notification ding at scene9 start + 0.2\n- success chime at scene9 + 3.6 (status flip)\n- soft whoosh at each scene boundary (subtle, low volume)\n\nLet me implement.\n\nAmplitude targets: final peak ~0.89, and RMS reasonable.\n\nVoice gain: narration normalized to peak 0.75, RMS ~ -18dB.\nBGM: about -26 dB RMS before ducking.\n\nDucking: compute voice envelope (abs, smoothed, resample), gain = 1 - 0.55*env_norm → BGM dips under speech.\n\nLet me write audio.py.\n\nDecoding narration: ffmpeg -i s01.mp3 -ar 48000 -ac 1 -f wav out.wav, then read with wave module.\n\nSimplest: use ffmpeg to output raw s16le and np.frombuffer.\n\nCommand: ffmpeg -v error -i X.mp3 -f s16le -acodec pcm_s16le -ac 1 -ar 48000 - \p gets piped\n\nI'll use subprocess.run with capture_output=True.\n\nWrite final wav with wave module (stereo 16-bit).\n\nThen mux with video using ffmpeg -i video.mp4 -i audio.wav -c:v copy -c:a aac -b:a 192k.\n\nLet me write.\n\nReverb implementation:\n```\ndef reverb(x, sr, taps=[(0.031,0.5),(0.057,0.35),(0.089,0.25),(0.131,0.18)]):\n    out = x.copy()\n    for d,g in taps:\n        n=int(d*sr)\n        y=np.zeros_like(x)\n        y[n:] = x[:-n]*g\n        out += y\n    return out\n```\nPlus a feedback comb maybe.\n\nLowpass one-pole:\n```\ndef lp(x, cutoff, sr):\n    a = math.exp(-2*math.pi*cutoff/sr)\n    y=np.zeros_like(x); acc=0.0\n    # vectorized via lfilter? no scipy. Use iterative? slow for 5M samples.\n```\nscipy may not be available. Iterative over 5.2M samples in Python is way too slow.\n\nAlternative: use FFT-based filtering — feasible with numpy. \nLowpass via FFT: multiply spectrum by a smooth rolloff. That's fine for pad/hats.\n\nOr use simple moving average (box filter) via np.convolve — fast enough with kernel ~small.\n\nI'll implement:\n- saw wave: sum of harmonics with 1/n amplitude up to Nyquist limit (band-limited additive) — avoids aliasing and no filter needed. Good.\n- For pad: additive with limited harmonics (e.g., 12 harmonics with 1/n^1.6) → soft.\n- For hats: white noise * envelope, then highpass via subtracting smoothed version (box filter with np.convolve, fast).\n- snare: noise + 180Hz tone.\n\nnp.convolve with large kernels on 5M samples: kernel 1000 → 5e9 ops, too slow. Use cumulative sum box filter (O(n)). Good: box_smooth via cumsum.\n\nFor highpass: x - box_smooth(x, window).\n\nOK let me write.\n\nPiano: additive harmonics with per-harmonic decay: sum over n of a_n * exp(-t*n*k) * sin(2π f n t). With ~8 harmonics per note and ~200 notes total, each note ~1s = 48000 samples * 8 = 384k ops per note → 200 notes = 77M ops. Acceptable (~1-2s numpy).\n\nBell voice for melody: FM: sin(2πfc t + I*exp(-t*3)*sin(2π fm t)) with decay.\n\nKick: sin(2π * f(t) * t) where f sweeps: use phase integration: f = 45 + 90*exp(-t*30); phase = cumsum(2π f /sr). Then * exp(-t*8).\n\nHat: noise * exp(-t*60) highpassed, 0.05s.\n\nSnare: noise*exp(-t*22) + sin(2π*190t)*exp(-t*30)*0.5.\n\nLet me write the code now. Also BGM stereo: create slight differences (pan pad slightly, delay right by 12ms for width).\n\nTotal samples = 109.52*48000 = 5,256,960. Float32 arrays of that size ~21MB each. Several layers ok.\n\nLet me write.\n\nI'll structure:\n\n```python\nSR=48000\nTOTAL=plan['total']\nN=int(TOTAL*SR)+SR\ndef midi(n): return 440*2**((n-69)/12)\n```\n\nChord table as list of dicts per bar with root and notes.\n\nThen:\n- pad_buf: for each bar, add chord notes as pads sustained through bar\n- bass_buf: per bar root, eighth-note pulses\n- arp_buf: per bar, notes arpeggiated 8th notes\n- bell_buf: melody per bar\n- drum_buf: kick/hat/snare\n\nThen sum with section-dependent gains via envelope arrays (simpler: build each layer only in its active window).\n\nLet me just gate each layer by bar index ranges.\n\nWrite it.\n\nAlso: narration placement offset +0.25s after scene start.\n\nVoice envelope for ducking: from the composed voice track.\n\nLet me write audio.py now.\n\nOne thing: the video is being rendered to video.mp4 simultaneously; audio.py reads plan.json (already written by render). Good.\n\nLet me write.🔧 调用工具: create_file\n参数: {"content": "# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\"\\"\\"音频工程：多轨 BGM + 音效 + 语音闪避 + 混音\\"\\"\\"\\nimport os, json, math, subprocess, wave\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nBASE = \\"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt\\"\\nSR = 48000\\n\\nwith open(os.path.join(BASE, \\"plan.json\\"), encoding=\\"utf-8\\") as f:\\n    PLAN = json.load(f)\\nTOTAL = PLAN[\\"total\\"]\\nSC = PLAN[\\"scenes\\"]\\nN = int(TOTAL * SR) + SR\\n\\nrng = np.random.default_rng(2026)\\ntt = np.arange(N, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n\\n\\ndef midi(n):\\n    return 440.0 * (2.0 ** ((n - 69) / 12.0))\\n\\n\\ndef env_exp(dur, k):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    return np.exp(-t * k).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef add(buf, start, sig, gain=1.0):\\n    i = int(start * SR)\\n    if i < 0 or i >= buf.shape[0]:\\n        return\\n    n = min(sig.shape[0], buf.shape[0] - i)\\n    if n > 0:\\n        buf[i:i + n] += sig[:n] * gain\\n\\n\\ndef pad_note(freq, dur, amp=0.1, bright=1.0):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\\n    for h in range(1, 13):\\n        f = freq * h\\n        if f > SR * 0.45:\\n            break\\n        s += (np.sin(2 * np.pi * f * t) / (h ** 1.65)).astype(np.float32)\\n    atk = np.clip(t / 0.45, 0, 1) ** 1.5\\n    rel = np.clip((dur - t) / 0.7, 0, 1)\\n    return (s * atk * rel * amp * bright).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef piano_note(freq, dur, amp=0.1):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\\n    for h in range(1, 9):\\n        f = freq * h\\n        if f > SR * 0.45:\\n            break\\n        s += (np.sin(2 * np.pi * f * t) * np.exp(-t * (2.6 + h * 1.5)) / h ** 1.1).astype(np.float32)\\n    s *= np.exp(-t * 1.1)\\n    atk = np.clip(t / 0.008, 0, 1)\\n    return (s * atk * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef bass_note(freq, dur, amp=0.2):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    s = np.sin(2 * np.pi * freq * t) + 0.32 * np.sin(4 * np.pi * freq * t) \\\\\\n        + 0.12 * np.sin(6 * np.pi * freq * t)\\n    atk = np.clip(t / 0.012, 0, 1)\\n    rel = np.clip((dur - t) / 0.12, 0, 1)\\n    return (s * atk * rel * np.exp(-t * 1.6) * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef bell_note(freq, dur, amp=0.12, idx=2.2):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    mod = idx * np.exp(-t * 3.2) * np.sin(2 * np.pi * freq * 2.01 * t)\\n    s = np.sin(2 * np.pi * freq * t + mod) * np.exp(-t * 2.0)\\n    atk = np.clip(t / 0.006, 0, 1)\\n    return (s * atk * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef box(x, w):\\n    w = max(1, int(w))\\n    c = np.cumsum(np.pad(x, (1, 0)), dtype=np.float64)\\n    y = (c[w:] - c[:-w]) / w\\n    return np.pad(y, (0, x.shape[0] - y.shape[0])).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef kick(amp=0.5, dur=0.32):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    f = 44 + 96 * np.exp(-t * 26)\\n    ph = 2 * np.pi * np.cumsum(f) / SR\\n    s = np.sin(ph) * np.exp(-t * 9)\\n    s[:int(0.004 * SR)] += rng.normal(0, 1, int(0.004 * SR)) * 0.25\\n    return (s * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef hat(amp=0.12, dur=0.06):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    nz = rng.normal(0, 1, n).astype(np.float32)\\n    nz = nz - box(nz, int(0.0016 * SR))\\n    return (nz * np.exp(-t * 75) * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef snare(amp=0.16, dur=0.22):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    nz = rng.normal(0, 1, n).astype(np.float32)\\n    nz = nz - box(nz, int(0.004 * SR))\\n    s = nz * np.exp(-t * 26) + 0.5 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 186 * t) * np.exp(-t * 42)\\n    return (s * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef thud(amp=0.45, dur=0.45):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    f = 70 + 60 * np.exp(-t * 18)\\n    ph = 2 * np.pi * np.cumsum(f) / SR\\n    s = np.sin(ph) * np.exp(-t * 7)\\n    nz = rng.normal(0, 1, n).astype(np.float32) * np.exp(-t * 40) * 0.3\\n    return ((s + nz) * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef ding(amp=0.3, dur=1.6):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    s = (np.sin(2 * np.pi * 1046.5 * t) * np.exp(-t * 2.2)\\n         + 0.6 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 1568 * t) * np.exp(-t * 3.0))\\n    return (s * np.clip(t / 0.004, 0, 1) * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef click(amp=0.1):\\n    n = int(0.02 * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    nz = rng.normal(0, 1, n).astype(np.float32)\\n    nz = nz - box(nz, int(0.0008 * SR))\\n    return (nz * np.exp(-t * 240) * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\ndef chime(amp=0.26):\\n    seq = [72, 76, 79, 84]\\n    out = np.zeros(int(2.2 * SR), dtype=np.float32)\\n    for i, m in enumerate(seq):\\n        s = bell_note(midi(m), 1.9 - i * 0.12, amp * (0.95 - 0.1 * i), 1.6)\\n        add(out, i * 0.10, s, 1.0)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef whoosh(amp=0.09, dur=0.7):\\n    n = int(dur * SR)\\n    t = np.arange(n, dtype=np.float32) / SR\\n    nz = rng.normal(0, 1, n).astype(np.float32)\\n    lo = box(nz, int(0.02 * SR))\\n    s = (nz - lo) * np.sin(np.pi * t / dur) ** 2\\n    return (s * amp).astype(np.float32)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------- 和弦与结构 ----------------\\nBAR = 60.0 / 92 * 4          # 2.6087s\\nNBAR = int(math.ceil(TOTAL / BAR)) + 1\\n\\nCH = {\\n    \\"Am\\": (45, [57, 60, 64]),\\n    \\"Fmaj7\\": (41, [53, 57, 60, 64]),\\n    \\"Dm\\": (50, [57, 62, 65]),\\n    \\"E\\": (40, [56, 59, 64]),\\n    \\"C\\": (48, [55, 59, 64, 67]),\\n    \\"G\\": (43, [55, 59, 62]),\\n    \\"Em\\": (52, [55, 59, 64]),\\n    \\"G/B\\": (47, [55, 59, 62]),\\n}\\nPROG = ([\\"Am\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\", \\"Am\\"] + [\\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\"] +\\n        [\\"Dm\\", \\"Am\\", \\"E\\", \\"Dm\\"] + [\\"E\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\", \\"Am\\"] +\\n        [\\"C\\", \\"G\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\"] + [\\"C\\", \\"G\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\"] +\\n        [\\"Fmaj7\\", \\"G\\", \\"Em\\", \\"Am\\"] + [\\"Fmaj7\\", \\"G\\", \\"Em\\", \\"Am\\"] +\\n        [\\"C\\", \\"G\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\"] + [\\"C\\", \\"G\\", \\"Am\\", \\"Fmaj7\\"] +\\n        [\\"Fmaj7\\", \\"G\\", \\"C\\", \\"C\\"] + [\\"C\\", \\"C\\", \\"C\\", \\"C\\"])\\n\\n\\ndef chord_at(bar):\\n    return CH[PROG[bar % len(PROG)]]\\n\\n\\npad = np.zeros(N, dtype=np.float32)\\nbas = np.zeros(N, dtype=np.float32)\\narp = np.zeros(N, dtype=np.float32)\\nmel = np.zeros(N, dtype=np.float32)\\ndrm = np.zeros(N, dtype=np.float32)\\n\\nfor b in range(NBAR):\\n    t0 = b * BAR\\n    if t0 > TOTAL:\\n        break\\n    root, notes = chord_at(b)\\n    # PAD\\n    pg = 0.9\\n    if b < 3:\\n        pg = 0.62\\n    if b > 36:\\n        pg = 0.72\\n    for k, m in enumerate(notes):\\n        add(pad, t0, pad_note(midi(m), BAR * 1.05, 0.085 * pg, 1.0), 1.0)\\n    add(pad, t0, pad_note(midi(root + 12), BAR * 1.05, 0.05 * pg, 0.9), 1.0)\\n\\n    # BASS —— 从第 2 小节进入，八分推进\\n    if 2 <= b <= 40:\\n        bg = 0.9 if b < 14 else 1.0\\n        step = BAR / 8\\n        for i in range(8):\\n            if b < 6 and i % 2 == 1:\\n                continue\\n            g = bg if (i % 4 == 0) else bg * 0.62\\n            add(bas, t0 + i * step, bass_note(midi(root), step * 0.92, 0.17 * g), 1.0)\\n\\n    # ARP —— 从第 10 小节进入\\n    if 10 <= b <= 40:\\n        step = BAR / 8\\n        pat = [0, 2, 1, 3, 2, 1, 3, 2]\\n        for i in range(8):\\n            m = notes[pat[i] % len(notes)] + 12\\n            g = 0.9 if i % 4 == 0 else 0.6\\n            add(arp, t0 + i * step, piano_note(midi(m), step * 3.2, 0.075 * g), 1.0)\\n\\n    # MELODY —— 18-37 小节\\n    if 18 <= b <= 37:\\n        top = [n + 24 for n in notes]\\n        seq = [top[0], top[-1], top[1], top[-1]]\\n        for i, m in enumerate(seq[:3]):\\n            if (b + i) % 3 == 1 and b % 2 == 1:\\n                continue\\n            add(mel, t0 + i * BAR / 3.0, bell_note(midi(m), 1.5, 0.085), 1.0)\\n\\n    # 鼓 —— 14 小节起\\n    if 14 <= b <= 38:\\n        strong = 30 <= b <= 38\\n        for i in range(4):\\n            bt = t0 + i * BAR / 4\\n            if b >= 18:\\n                add(drm, bt, kick(0.34 if strong else 0.24), 1.0)\\n            if b >= 18:\\n                for j in range(2):\\n                    add(drm, bt + j * BAR / 8, hat(0.075 if strong else 0.05), 1.0)\\n            if strong and i % 2 == 1:\\n                add(drm, bt, snare(0.11), 1.0)\\n\\n# 整体动态弧线\\narc = np.ones(N, dtype=np.float32)\\nsegs = [(0, 8, 0.55), (8, 23, 0.7), (23, 42, 0.85), (42, 64, 1.0),\\n        (64, 87, 0.95), (87, 100, 0.9), (100, TOTAL, 0.62)]\\nx = tt\\nfor a, b2, g in segs:\\n    arc[(x >= a) & (x < b2)] = g\\narc = np.convolve(arc, np.ones(int(0.8 * SR)) / int(0.8 * SR), mode=\\"same\\").astype(np.float32)\\narc[int((TOTAL - 4.5) * SR):] *= np.linspace(1, 0, N - int((TOTAL - 4.5) * SR)) ** 0.9\\narc[:int(1.5 * SR)] *= np.linspace(0, 1, int(1.5 * SR)) ** 0.8\\n\\nbgm = (pad * 0.95 + bas * 0.8 + arp * 0.72 + mel * 0.55 + drm * 0.5) * arc\\n\\n# 混响（多抽头 + 反馈梳）\\ndef reverb(x, dly=0.037, fb=0.42, taps=((0.031, 0.42), (0.059, 0.3), (0.097, 0.22), (0.149, 0.15))):\\n    out = x.astype(np.float32).copy()\\n    for d, g in taps:\\n        n = int(d * SR)\\n        if n < x.shape[0]:\\n            y = np.zeros_like(x)\\n            y[n:] = x[:-n] * g\\n            out += y\\n    return out * 0.72\\n\\n\\nbgm = reverb(bgm, taps=((0.029, 0.34), (0.053, 0.24), (0.091, 0.17), (0.137, 0.11)))\\nbgm = bgm / (np.abs(bgm).max() + 1e-9) * 0.62\\n\\n# 立体声加宽\\nbgmR = np.roll(bgm, int(0.011 * SR)) * 0.95\\nbgmL = bgm * 1.0\\n\\n# ---------------- 音效 ----------------\\nsfx = np.zeros((2, N), dtype=np.float32)\\nfor s in SC:\\n    add(sfx[0], s[\\"start\\"] + 0.02, whoosh(0.045), 1.0)\\n    add(sfx[1], s[\\"start\\"] + 0.02, whoosh(0.045), 1.0)\\n\\n# 场景 2 封禁弹窗：低频撞击\\nadd(sfx[0], SC[1][\\"start\\"] + 0.35, thud(0.5), 1.0)\\nadd(sfx[1], SC[1][\\"start\\"] + 0.35, thud(0.5), 1.0)\\n# 场景 3 三个错误动作：三下轻微警示\\nfor i in range(3):\\n    add(sfx[0], SC[2][\\"start\\"] + 0.55 + i * 0.85, thud(0.16, 0.18), 1.0)\\n    add(sfx[1], SC[2][\\"start\\"] + 0.55 + i * 0.85, thud(0.16, 0.18), 1.0)\\n# 场景 6 / 7 键盘打字声\\nfor i in range(22):\\n    p = SC[5][\\"start\\"] + 0.5 + i * 0.062\\n    add(sfx[0], p, click(0.055), 1.0)\\n    add(sfx[1], p, click(0.045), 1.0)\\nfor i in range(26):\\n    p = SC[6][\\"start\\"] + 1.0 + i * 0.155\\n    add(sfx[0], p, click(0.042), 1.0)\\n    add(sfx[1], p, click(0.035), 1.0)\\n# 场景 9 通知 + 成功和弦\\nadd(sfx[0], SC[8][\\"start\\"] + 0.25, ding(0.28), 1.0)\\nadd(sfx[1], SC[8][\\"start\\"] + 0.28, ding(0.26), 1.0)\\nch = chime(0.24)\\nadd(sfx[0], SC[8][\\"start\\"] + 3.6, ch, 1.0)\\nadd(sfx[1], SC[8][\\"start\\"] + 3.63, ch, 1.0)\\n\\nbgm = np.stack([bgmL, bgmR])\\n\\n# ---------------- 人声 ----------------\\nvoice = np.zeros((2, N), dtype=np.float32)\\nVO_OFF = 0.22\\nfor s in SC:\\n    sid = s[\\"id\\"]\\n    p = os.path.join(BASE, \\"aud\\", sid + \\".mp3\\")\\n    r = subprocess.run([\\"ffmpeg\\", \\"-v\\", \\"error\\", \\"-i\\", p, \\"-f\\", \\"s16le\\",\\n                        \\"-acodec\\", \\"pcm_s16le\\", \\"-ac\\", \\"1\\", \\"-ar\\", str(SR), \\"-\\"],\\n                       capture_output=True)\\n    a = np.frombuffer(r.stdout, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\\n    if a.size == 0:\\n        continue\\n    a = a / (np.abs(a).max() + 1e-9) * 0.86\\n    # 轻微低切 + 高频柔化\\n    a = a - box(a, int(0.0009 * SR))\\n    add(voice[0], s[\\"start\\"] + VO_OFF, a, 1.0)\\n    add(voice[1], s[\\"start\\"] + VO_OFF, a, 1.0)\\n\\n# 语音闪避：人声越大，BGM 越低\\nenv = np.abs(voice[0])\\nenv = box(env, int(0.09 * SR))\\nenv = env / (env.max() + 1e-9)\\nduck = 1.0 - 0.62 * np.clip(env * 3.2, 0, 1)\\nbgm = bgm * duck[None, :]\\n\\nmix = bgm * 0.52 + sfx * 0.85 + voice * 1.0\\n\\n# 总线：软限幅\\nmix = np.tanh(mix * 1.06) * 0.94\\nmix = mix / (np.abs(mix).max() + 1e-9) * 0.93\\n\\nout = os.path.join(BASE, \\"audio.wav\\")\\nwith wave.open(out, \\"wb\\") as w:\\n    w.setnchannels(2)\\n    w.setsampwidth(2)\\n    w.setframerate(SR)\\n    w.writeframes((mix.T[:int(TOTAL * SR)] * 32767).astype(np.int16).tobytes())\\n\\nrms = np.sqrt((mix ** 2).mean())\\nprint(\\"AUDIO_OK %.2fs  RMS %.1f dBFS  PEAK %.1f dBFS\\" %\\n      (TOTAL, 20 * np.log10(rms + 1e-9), 20 * np.log10(np.abs(mix).max() + 1e-9)))\\n", "path": "/data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/audio.py"}\n结果: ✅ 创建 /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/audio.py (11485 字节)\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && tail -4 render.log; echo \\"--- frames done: $(ls -l video.mp4 2>/dev/null \p awk '{print $5}') bytes\\"", "timeout": 60}\n结果: TOTAL 109.520s  FRAMES 6571\nFRAME 0/6571  0.0%\nFRAME 164/6571  2.5%\nFRAME 328/6571  5.0%\n--- frames done: 553322 bytes\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && time python3 audio.py 2>&1 \p tail -6", "timeout": 600}\n结果: sh: 1: time: not found\n\n\n`time` not available. Run without it.\n\nVideo render at 5% after some time. Let's run audio.py.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 audio.py 2>&1 \p tail -8", "timeout": 900}\n结果: AUDIO_OK 109.52s  RMS -19.9 dBFS  PEAK -0.6 dBFS\n\n\nAudio built: RMS -19.9 dBFS, peak -0.6 dBFS. Good.\n\nLet me verify audio content: check that voice is audible at scene starts and BGM present throughout. Let me analyze segments: compute RMS in speech windows vs silence windows.\n\nAlso check no clipping (peak -0.6 fine).\n\nLet me check video progress too.\n\nLet me do an analysis: for each scene, measure RMS in the narration window (should be high ~-16dB) and check that in gaps there's only BGM (~-30dB).\n\nAlso verify spectral content of BGM (not silence).\n\nLet me run a quick analysis script.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport wave, numpy as np, json\\nw=wave.open('audio.wav'); n=w.getnframes(); sr=w.getframerate()\\na=np.frombuffer(w.readframes(n),dtype=np.int16).reshape(-1,2).astype(np.float32)/32768.0\\nm=a.mean(axis=1)\\nplan=json.load(open('plan.json'))\\ndef rms(x): return 20*np.log10(np.sqrt((x**2).mean())+1e-9)\\nprint(\\"总时长 %.2fs 声道数 %d\\"%(n/sr, a.shape[1]))\\nprint(\\"\\\\n场景人声窗口 (应≈-14~-20dB):\\")\\nfor i,s in enumerate(plan['scenes']):\\n    t0=int((s['start']+0.22)*sr); t1=int((s['start']+0.22+s['narr']*0.85)*sr)\\n    print(\\"  %s %-22s %6.1f dB\\"%(s['id'],s['label'],rms(m[t0:t1])))\\nprint(\\"\\\\n场景间隙 仅有BGM (应≈-28~-38dB):\\")\\nfor i,s in enumerate(plan['scenes'][:-1]):\\n    t0=int((s['start']+s['dur']-0.45)*sr); t1=int((s['start']+s['dur'])*sr)\\n    print(\\"  gap%02d %6.1f dB\\"%(i,rms(m[t0:t1])))\\nprint(\\"\\\\n尾部淡出 %6.1f dB\\"%rms(m[-int(2.5*sr):]))\\nEOF", "timeout": 180}\n结果: 总时长 109.52s 声道数 2\n\n场景人声窗口 (应≈-14~-20dB):\n  s01 夜 · 提交之前                -19.5 dB\n  s02 提示 · 账号已停用              -20.0 dB\n  s03 误区 · 三个错误动作             -20.3 dB\n  s04 冷静 · 先分清类型              -20.5 dB\n  s05 自查 · 你是哪一种              -19.8 dB\n  s06 入口 · 正确的位置              -19.9 dB\n  s07 话术 · 只讲事实               -19.4 dB\n  s08 等待 · 别重复开单              -19.2 dB\n  s09 结果 · 误判被纠正              -20.4 dB\n  s10 结论 · 申诉的本质              -22.0 dB\n\n场景间隙 仅有BGM (应≈-28~-38dB):\n  gap00  -28.6 dB\n  gap01  -29.7 dB\n  gap02  -26.1 dB\n  gap03  -26.0 dB\n  gap04  -24.8 dB\n  gap05  -20.0 dB\n  gap06  -22.8 dB\n  gap07  -23.8 dB\n  gap08  -25.0 dB\n\n尾部淡出  -38.9 dB\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && tail -3 render.log", "timeout": 60}\n结果: FRAME 0/6571  0.0%\nFRAME 164/6571  2.5%\nFRAME 328/6571  5.0%\n\n\nAudio distribution looks good: voice ~-19 to -20dB, gaps BGM -20 to -30dB. Hmm gap05 is -20.0 dB which equals voice level — that's because gap window includes tail of narration? I used s['start']+s['dur']-0.45 to end; narration ends at start+0.22+narr, and dur=narr+0.7 so narration ends 0.48 before dur end. So the window -0.45..0 overlaps the last 0.03s of narration... mostly BGM. But -20dB seems loud for BGM alone. gap05 is after scene 6 (index 5). Hmm the BGM at that point has drums+arp, could be -20dB RMS. That might be too loud relative to voice at -19.9. \n\nActually BGM at -20dB RMS vs voice -20dB RMS → BGM would compete. Ducking should have reduced it, but in gaps ducking is off so BGM returns to full. If BGM full level is -20dB RMS, that's too loud for background.\n\nWait, mix = bgm*0.52 + voice. Total was normalized to peak 0.93. If BGM RMS after 0.52 gain is -20dB... Let me measure separately: compute BGM alone RMS. I didn't save it. \n\nHmm, but the perceived issue: BGM in gaps at -20dB is fairly loud but not crazy; typical background music under narration sits around -25 to -30 dB RMS. -20 dB is loud-ish but the user complained before about "太单调" not "太响". Still, for a tutorial with voice, BGM at -20 could compete.\n\nLet me reduce BGM a bit: change `mix = bgm * 0.52 + ...` to 0.40, and increase ducking depth. Actually ducking already 0.62 reduction.\n\nBetter approach: measure BGM-only RMS and voice-only RMS, then set gains so voice RMS ≈ -18dB and BGM RMS ≈ -28dB.\n\nLet me modify audio.py: after computing tracks, compute normalization explicitly:\n- voice_norm: scale voice so its RMS (over speech-active regions) = -18 dBFS\n- bgm_norm: scale bgm so its RMS = -28 dBFS\n- Then mix.\n\nActually the final normalization to peak 0.93 overrides. Let me do:\n1. voice → RMS over active regions = -17 dBFS, peak < 0.85\n2. bgm → RMS = -27 dBFS\n3. mix, then if peak > 0.95 apply tanh soft limit gently.\n\nSince peak already -0.6 dBFS with normalization to 0.93 — that means the signal is peaky. Normalizing to peak 0.93 and getting RMS -19.9 means crest factor ~19dB, fine.\n\nIf I instead target voice RMS -17 and BGM -27, mix peak might exceed 1 → use soft limiter.\n\nLet me restructure: \n- compute voice_rms_target scaling\n- compute bgm scaling\n- mix = voice*gs + bgm*gb*duck + sfx*gsf\n- soft clip with tanh at level slightly above, then peak normalize to 0.95.\n\nGiven tanh compresses peaks, RMS will end around -19, acceptable. But then BGM relative will be preserved. Good.\n\nLet me tune: voice RMS target -17.5 dBFS (loud clear narration), BGM RMS -28.5 dBFS → 11 dB below voice. In gaps BGM alone = -28.5 dB → good background level.\n\nCurrently gaps are -20 to -26, so need ~6-8dB reduction on BGM. Setting explicit targets fixes it.\n\nLet me patch audio.py's mixing section.\n\nAlso sfx should be modest: -30dB peak-ish.\n\nLet me rewrite the mixing block:\n\n```python\n# 人声按有效区间定标\nact = voice[0][np.abs(voice[0]) > 0.02]\nv_rms = np.sqrt((act**2).mean()) if act.size else 0.1\ngv = 10**(-17.5/20) / (v_rms+1e-9)\n# BGM 定标\nb_rms = np.sqrt((bgm[0]**2).mean())\ngb = 10**(-28.5/20) / (b_rms+1e-9)\n# SFX\ns_rms = np.sqrt((sfx[0]**2).mean())\ngs = 10**(-31.0/20) / (s_rms+1e-9)\n\nmix = voice*gv + bgm*gb*duck + sfx*gs\n# 软限幅\npk = np.abs(mix).max()\nif pk > 0.9: mix = np.tanh(mix/pk*1.4)*0.92/np.tanh(1.4)\n```\nHmm tanh scaling: let me do simpler:\n```\nmix = mix / max(1.0, pk/0.92)\nmix = np.tanh(mix*1.05)*0.95\n```\nThen measure.\n\nLet me patch and re-run audio (fast, ~1-2 min). Video still rendering.\n\nNote bgm array is 2xN and duck is 1D → bgm*gb*duck[None,:] fine.\n\nLet me apply.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\np='audio.py'\\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\\nold_start = s.index(\\"mix = bgm * 0.52 + sfx * 0.85 + voice * 1.0\\")\\nold_end = s.index(\\"out = os.path.join(BASE, \\\\\\"audio.wav\\\\\\")\\")\\nnew = '''# ---------------- 按绝对电平定标 ----------------\\ndef db2lin(d):\\n    return 10.0 ** (d / 20.0)\\n\\nact = voice[0][np.abs(voice[0]) > 0.02]\\nv_rms = float(np.sqrt((act ** 2).mean())) if act.size else 0.1\\ngv = db2lin(-17.5) / (v_rms + 1e-9)\\n\\nb_rms = float(np.sqrt((bgm[0] ** 2).mean()))\\ngb = db2lin(-28.5) / (b_rms + 1e-9)\\n\\ns_rms = float(np.sqrt((sfx[0] ** 2).mean()))\\ngs = db2lin(-30.0) / (s_rms + 1e-9)\\n\\nmix = voice * gv + bgm * gb * duck[None, :] + sfx * gs\\n\\npk = float(np.abs(mix).max())\\nif pk > 0.0:\\n    mix = mix / pk * 1.06\\nmix = np.tanh(mix) * 0.95\\nmix = mix / (np.abs(mix).max() + 1e-9) * 0.95\\n\\n'''\\ns = s[:old_start] + new + s[old_end:]\\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint(\\"patched\\")\\nPYEOF\\npython3 audio.py 2>&1 \p tail -4", "timeout": 900}\n结果: patched\nAUDIO_OK 109.52s  RMS -21.1 dBFS  PEAK -0.4 dBFS\n\n\nNow verify distribution again.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport wave, numpy as np, json\\nw=wave.open('audio.wav'); n=w.getnframes(); sr=w.getframerate()\\na=np.frombuffer(w.readframes(n),dtype=np.int16).reshape(-1,2).astype(np.float32)/32768.0\\nm=a.mean(axis=1); plan=json.load(open('plan.json'))\\ndef rms(x): return 20*np.log10(np.sqrt((x**2).mean())+1e-9)\\nv=[];g=[]\\nfor s in plan['scenes']:\\n    t0=int((s['start']+0.3)*sr); t1=int((s['start']+0.2+s['narr']*0.8)*sr)\\n    v.append(rms(m[t0:t1]))\\nfor s in plan['scenes'][:-1]:\\n    t0=int((s['start']+s['dur']-0.5)*sr); t1=int((s['start']+s['dur']-0.06)*sr)\\n    g.append(rms(m[t0:t1]))\\nprint(\\"人声区间 dB:\\", \\" \\".join(\\"%.1f\\"%x for x in v))\\nprint(\\"间隙BGM  dB:\\", \\" \\".join(\\"%.1f\\"%x for x in g))\\nprint(\\"人声均值 %.1f  间隙均值 %.1f  差值 %.1f dB\\"%(np.mean(v),np.mean(g),np.mean(v)-np.mean(g)))\\nprint(\\"声道差异(立体声): %.4f\\"%(np.abs(a[:,0]-a[:,1]).mean()))\\nEOF", "timeout": 180}\n结果: 人声区间 dB: -19.7 -19.9 -20.5 -21.5 -20.8 -21.2 -20.3 -19.7 -20.4 -22.9\n间隙BGM  dB: -32.9 -34.1 -30.4 -30.8 -29.0 -24.2 -27.0 -27.7 -29.2\n人声均值 -20.7  间隙均值 -29.5  差值 8.8 dB\n声道差异(立体声): 0.0382\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && tail -2 render.log", "timeout": 60}\n结果: FRAME 164/6571  2.5%\nFRAME 328/6571  5.0%\n\n\nNow voice -20.7 avg, BGM -29.5 → 8.8 dB separation. Good.\n\nBut the render log hasn't progressed past 5% — that's suspicious. It printed FRAME 328/6571 at 5%. The log updates every 164 frames. Let me check if process is alive and how many frames processed. It's been a few minutes. 6571 frames at 37ms = 4 min. Let me check process status and video.mp4 size growth.\n\nEarlier video.mp4 was 553322 bytes at 5%. Let me check now.\n\nAlso possible: printing every 164 frames but pipe buffering. Let me check process CPU.\n\nLet me check.🔧 调用工具: batch_command\n参数: {"commands": ["ps -A -o PID,ETIME,%%CPU,ARGS \p grep -E 'python3\pffmpeg' \p grep -v grep", "ls -l ~/vt/video.mp4; wc -l ~/vt/render.log"], "timeout": 60}\n结果: 批量执行 2 条命令：\nerror: improper AIX field descriptor\n\nUsage:\n ps [options]\n\n Try 'ps --help <simple\plist\poutput\pthreads\pmisc\pall>'\n  or 'ps --help <s\pl\po\pt\pm\pa>'\n for additional help text.\n\nFor more details see ps(1).\n-rw-------. 1 u0_a1308 u0_a1308 553322 Nov  1 15:14 /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/video.mp4\n4 /data/data/com.termux/files/home/vt/render.log\n\n\nvideo.mp4 is 553322 bytes and not growing since 15:14. Current time? Let me check. The render may have stalled or died.\n\nLet me check processes with list_processes tool and check log content fully.\n\nPossibly the background process died when I ran other commands? Or ffmpeg's stdout DEVNULL and stderr pipe filled up → deadlock! Yes: I set stderr=subprocess.PIPE and never read it until the end. ffmpeg writes progress to stderr; if the pipe buffer (64KB) fills, ffmpeg blocks → render stalls. That's exactly the classic bug.\n\nFix: stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL (or to a file).\n\nLet me kill the process and re-run with stderr to a file.\n\nLet me check processes first.🔧 调用工具: list_processes\n参数: {"filter": "ffmpeg"}\n结果: (无匹配进程)\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && cat render.log; date", "timeout": 30}\n结果: TOTAL 109.520s  FRAMES 6571\nFRAME 0/6571  0.0%\nFRAME 164/6571  2.5%\nFRAME 328/6571  5.0%\nSun Nov  1 15:20:25 CST 2026\n\n\nBoth python3 and ffmpeg are gone. So the process died/was killed. Probably OOM killer or the background task got killed when the parent shell exited.\n\nHmm, video.mp4 is 553KB partial. The process ended. Log has no error.\n\nPossible cause: the background process was killed (Termux background, phantom process killer!). The system prompt mentions Phantom Process Killer. Or it was killed because run_background's parent exited.\n\nBetter approach: run it in a way that survives — use nohup + setsid, or just run in foreground with a longer timeout. The full render takes ~4-5 min; I can run it in foreground with timeout 900.\n\nRisk: execute_command timeout. Let me run in foreground with timeout 900s and no stderr pipe (fix that too). 4-5 min should fit.\n\nLet me fix the stderr issue first, then run in foreground.\n\nAlso to be safe, add tmux? Simpler: foreground call.\n\nFix: stderr=open(logpath,'wb') so no pipe blockage.\n\nLet me patch and run in foreground.\n\nAlso enable wake lock? Could help avoid sleep interruptions. Let me acquire termux-wake-lock if available.\n\nLet me patch render.py: stderr to file.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\np='render.py'\\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\\ns=s.replace('''    proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdin=subprocess.PIPE,\\n                            stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)''',\\n'''    errf = open(os.path.join(BASE, \\"ffmpeg.log\\"), \\"wb\\")\\n    proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdin=subprocess.PIPE,\\n                            stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=errf)''')\\ns=s.replace('''    proc.stdin.close()\\n    err = proc.stderr.read().decode(\\"utf-8\\", \\"ignore\\")\\n    rc = proc.wait()''','''    proc.stdin.close()\\n    rc = proc.wait()\\n    errf.close()\\n    err = \\"\\"\\n    try:\\n        err = open(os.path.join(BASE, \\"ffmpeg.log\\"), \\"rb\\").read().decode(\\"utf-8\\", \\"ignore\\")\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass''')\\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint(\\"patched\\")\\nPYEOF\\ncommand -v termux-wake-lock && termux-wake-lock && echo \\"wakelock acquired\\"; rm -f ~/vt/video.mp4", "timeout": 60}\n结果: patched\n/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/termux-wake-lock\nwakelock acquired\n\n\nNow run render in foreground with timeout 900.\n\nEstimate: 6571 frames * 37ms = 243s + encode overhead. Should finish in ~5 min.\n\nLet me run.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && python3 render.py 2>&1 \p tail -6; echo \\"=== EXIT\\"; ls -l video.mp4", "timeout": 1500}\n结果: FRAME 5904/6571  89.8%\nFRAME 6068/6571  92.3%\nFRAME 6232/6571  94.8%\nFRAME 6396/6571  97.3%\nFRAME 6560/6571  99.8%\nFFMPEG_RC 0\n=== EXIT\n-rw-------. 1 u0_a1308 u0_a1308 9667570 Nov  1 15:29 video.mp4\n\n\nVideo rendered: 9.67 MB. Now mux with audio.\n\nThen verify with ffprobe, extract frames from the final video and OCR, and check audio.\n\nLet me mux.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && ffmpeg -y -v error -i video.mp4 -i audio.wav -map 0:v:0 -map 1:a:0 -c:v copy -c:a aac -b:a 192k -ar 48000 -ac 2 -movflags +faststart -shortest final.mp4 2>&1 \p tail -5; echo \\"=== rc=$?\\"; ls -l final.mp4; ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration,size,bit_rate -show_entries stream=codec_name,codec_type,width,height,r_frame_rate,nb_frames,sample_rate,channels -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 final.mp4", "timeout": 600}\n结果: === rc=0\n-rw-------. 1 u0_a1308 u0_a1308 12471088 Nov  1 15:29 final.mp4\ncodec_name=h264\ncodec_type=video\nwidth=1920\nheight=1080\nr_frame_rate=60/1\nnb_frames=6571\ncodec_name=aac\ncodec_type=audio\nsample_rate=48000\nchannels=2\nr_frame_rate=0/0\nnb_frames=5134\nduration=109.516667\nsize=12471088\nbit_rate=910991\n\n\nFinal: 1920x1080, 60fps, 6571 frames, 109.52s, AAC 48kHz stereo, 12.47MB.\n\nNow verify from the FINAL video (not intermediate): extract frames at various times and OCR; check audio present; check narrative presence.\n\nLet me extract frames at 10 points and OCR key text, plus verify audio track has voice at those times.\n\nThen copy to Download, cleanup, media scan, screen off/on.\n\nLet me do verification.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && mkdir -p chk && for t in 5 16 27 37 48 58 70 82 92 103; do ffmpeg -y -v error -ss $t -i final.mp4 -frames:v 1 chk/f$t.png 2>/dev/null; done; ls chk \p wc -l; for t in 5 16 27 37 48 58 70 82 92 103; do echo \\"== t=${t}s\\"; tesseract chk/f$t.png - -l chi_sim+eng --psm 11 2>/dev/null \p tr -s '\\\\n ' ' ' \p head -c 300; echo; done", "timeout": 600}\n结果: 10\n== t=5s\nGITHUB 账号解雪 实操指南 (1) WAL % - 提交之前 02:00 AM - 截止前6小时 e nn e 目 四 [N in nn [ e e 目 \p nn e e e 目 \p [ e e in e e e [ B ] in e e e e e nn 登录 GitHub ，准备提交毕业设计 \n== t=16s\n02 /10 GITHUB 账号解雪 实操指南 提示 账号已停\p (X X github.com/settings/profile . Your account has been suspended 您的账号已被停 违反《可接受使用政策》 UNAVAILABLE UNAVAILABLE UNAVAILABLE UNAVAILABLE 三年积累，一瞬间全部变灰 \n== t=27s\n03 /10 GITHUB 账号解封， 实操指南 误区 