\nimport numpy as np, json\\nsr=48000\\na=np.fromfile('aud_chk.raw',dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32)/32768.0\\nplan=json.load(open('plan.json'))\\ndef rms(x): return 20*np.log10(np.sqrt((x**2).mean())+1e-9)\\nprint(\\"音频总长 %.2fs\\"%(a.size/sr))\\nprint(\\"\\\\n各场景语音段实测:\\")\\nfor s in plan['scenes']:\\n    t0=int((s['start']+0.3)*sr); t1=int((s['start']+0.2+s['narr']*0.8)*sr)\\n    print(\\"  %s %.1f dB\\"%(s['id'],rms(a[t0:t1])))\\nprint(\\"\\\\n音效点核查:\\")\\nfor name,t in [(\\"通知音(S9)\\",plan['scenes'][8]['start']+0.25),(\\"成功和弦(S9)\\",plan['scenes'][8]['start']+3.6),(\\"封禁撞击(S2)\\",plan['scenes'][1]['start']+0.35)]:\\n    w=a[int((t-0.15)*sr):int((t+0.15)*sr)]\\n    print(\\"  %-14s 局部RMS %.1f dB  峰值 %.1f dB\\"%(name,rms(w),20*np.log10(np.abs(w).max()+1e-9)))\\nEOF", "timeout": 600}\n结果: 音频总长 109.50s\n\n各场景语音段实测:\n  s01 -19.7 dB\n  s02 -19.9 dB\n  s03 -20.5 dB\n  s04 -21.5 dB\n  s05 -20.8 dB\n  s06 -21.2 dB\n  s07 -20.3 dB\n  s08 -19.8 dB\n  s09 -20.5 dB\n  s10 -22.9 dB\n\n音效点核查:\n  通知音(S9)        局部RMS -18.0 dB  峰值 -6.1 dB\n  成功和弦(S9)       局部RMS -18.0 dB  峰值 -6.0 dB\n  封禁撞击(S2)       局部RMS -11.9 dB  峰值 -1.0 dB\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && for t in 45.0 45.5 46.0; do ffmpeg -y -v error -ss $t -i final.mp4 -frames:v 1 chk/m$t.png 2>/dev/null; done && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nimport numpy as np\\na=[np.asarray(Image.open('chk/m%s.png'%t).convert('L'),dtype=np.float32) for t in ['45.0','45.5','46.0']]\\nfor i in range(2):\\n    d=np.abs(a[i+1]-a[i])\\n    print(\\"帧间差异 45.%d→45.%d : 平均%.2f  变化像素%.2f%%\\"%(i*5,(i+1)*5,d.mean(),(d>6).mean()*100))\\nEOF", "timeout": 300}\n结果: 帧间差异 45.0→45.5 : 平均0.53  变化像素0.80%\n帧间差异 45.5→45.10 : 平均0.37  变化像素0.34%\n\n\nAudio verified: all 10 scenes have voice at -19 to -23 dB, SFX audible.\n\nFrame diff: only 0.8% pixels changing between frames 0.5s apart at t=45. That's low — animation is subtle. At t=45 (scene 5, lt=2.5) the checklist rows appear at 0.7,1.45,2.2,2.95 — so between 45.0 and 45.5 row 3 appears. Hmm 0.8% change. Particles + blobs should change more.\n\nThe blobs move slowly (sin(t*0.16)), particles drift. Between 0.5s: particle moves 8-26px/s*0.5 = 4-13px. Small dots 5-16px → some change.\n\nOnly 0.8% of pixels change. Visually the background is mostly static-ish. The user asked for "动画更加炫酷". Hmm. Animations exist (text reveals, cards sliding, typing, timeline progress, particles) but between two arbitrary frames within a settled moment, little changes.\n\nLet me check a moment with more motion: scene 3 cards popping (t≈24), scene 6 typing (t≈56).\n\nActually let me measure with 1-frame (1/60s) difference too — that's the meaningful "is it animated" metric. Between 0.5s apart at a quiet moment, little changes is normal.\n\nBut to be safe about "够不够炫", the design has: drifting light blobs, 46 particles, text fade/slide reveals, card slide-ins, red pulse vignette in S3, typing carets, timeline progress, rotating spinner, stamp scale-in, status chip flip, bell/chime audio. That's a decent amount.\n\nLet me quantify differently: measure frame-to-frame change over the whole video at several points, and also measure cumulative change over 2s windows.\n\nI think it's fine. But let me add a bit more ambient motion? That would require re-render (5 min). Given budget, maybe acceptable improvement: strengthen particle motion and add a slow scanning highlight. Hmm.\n\nThe user's key complaints: 无剧情/无动画/无配音/时长不够/分辨率低. We now have all. Rather than over-engineer, verify motion at active moments.\n\nLet me check t=24.5 vs 25.0 (S3 cards) and t=56.0 vs 56.3 (S6 typing).\n\nThen deliver.\n\nActually let me just check a couple and move on.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && for t in 24.2 24.7 55.8 56.2 90.5 91.0; do ffmpeg -y -v error -ss $t -i final.mp4 -frames:v 1 chk/a$t.png 2>/dev/null; done && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nimport numpy as np\\npairs=[('24.2','24.7','S3 卡片弹入+红脉冲'),('55.8','56.2','S6 地址栏打字'),('90.5','91.0','S9 状态翻转+邮件滑入')]\\nfor a,b,label in pairs:\\n    x=np.asarray(Image.open('chk/a%s.png'%a).convert('L'),dtype=np.float32)\\n    y=np.asarray(Image.open('chk/a%s.png'%b).convert('L'),dtype=np.float32)\\n    d=np.abs(y-x)\\n    print(\\"%-24s 平均差%5.2f  变化像素%5.2f%%\\"%(label,d.mean(),(d>6).mean()*100))\\nEOF", "timeout": 300}\n结果: S3 卡片弹入+红脉冲              平均差 1.34  变化像素 3.15%\nS6 地址栏打字                 平均差 0.35  变化像素 3.14%\nS9 状态翻转+邮件滑入             平均差 0.34  变化像素 0.49%\n\n\nAnimation confirmed at active moments (3% pixels changing per 0.5s). Fine.\n\nNow: copy to Download, cleanup temp files, media scan, and screen off/on.\n\nTarget filename: keep same name? User said "把该视频进行全面优化" — this replaces the previous. I'll write to Download with an upgraded name to make clear it's the new version, and delete the old 720p one? The user asked to optimize the video and upgrade to 1080p60. Previous file was github_unblock_tutorial_720p.mp4. I'll produce github_unblock_tutorial_1080p60.mp4 and remove the old 720p file (it's my own previously generated file → allowed to delete since I generated it).\n\nLet me copy, verify, delete old, clean temp dir (keep dir, delete files), media scan, then screen off/on.\n\nFiles I generated: ~/vt/* (aud/*.mp3, test/*.png, chk/*.png, *.wav, *.raw, video.mp4, various .py/.json/.log). All mine → delete files. Keep directories? The rule says don't delete directories. So delete files inside; leave empty dirs.\n\nActually rule: "你只能去删除文件，你不得删除目录". So use find -type f -delete within ~/vt.\n\nLet me do the copy + verify first.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/vt && cp final.mp4 /storage/emulated/0/Download/github_unblock_tutorial_1080p60.mp4 && rm -f /storage/emulated/0/Download/github_unblock_tutorial_720p.mp4 && ls -l /storage/emulated/0/Download/github_unblock*; echo \\"--- MD5 比对 ---\\"; md5sum final.mp4 /storage/emulated/0/Download/github_unblock_tutorial_1080p60.mp4", "timeout": 300}\n结果: -rw-rw----. 1 root everybody 12471088 Nov  1