t; delete it as it's my temp file).\n\nThen screen off → on.\n\nLet's do it.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"input keyevent 4; input keyevent 4\\"; sleep 1; cd ~ && rm -f alishot.png ali_top.png ali_full2x.png ali_tsv.tsv bal.png bal2x.png my.png my2x.png my_tsv.tsv bal2.png bal2_2x.png bal2_3x.png b_tsv.tsv c1.png c2.png c3.png; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"rm -f /sdcard/ui.xml\\"; ls ~/*.png ~/*.tsv 2>/dev/null; echo \\"清理完成\\"; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"ls /sdcard/ui.xml 2>&1\\"", "timeout": 60}\n结果: 清理完成\nls: /sdcard/ui.xml: No such file or directory\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"dumpsys window \p grep mCurrentFocus \p head -2; settings get system accelerometer_rotation; input keyevent 26; sleep 2; dumpsys power \p grep -E 'mWakefulness=' \p head -1; input keyevent 26; sleep 2; dumpsys power \p grep -E 'mWakefulness=' \p head -1\\"", "timeout": 60}\n结果:   mCurrentFocus=Window{7585f38 u0 com.eg.android.AlipayGphone/com.eg.android.AlipayGphone.AlipayLogin}\n1\n  mWakefulness=Asleep\n  mWakefulness=Awake\n\n\nWait — accelerometer_rotation returned 1! It was 0 earlier. Did something turn it on? I didn't change it. Hmm — maybe the keyevent 26 (power) with rotation? No. Perhaps Alipay or system auto-enabled? Or maybe reading order: the settings get ran after keyevent 26? No, order was: dumpsys focus; settings get; input keyevent 26...\n\nIt read 1. Earlier it was 0. Something turned auto-rotate on. Per the hard rule, I must turn it off. Let me set accelerometer_rotation 0.\n\nWait, could this "1" be a leftover? Let me just set it to 0 and verify.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"settings put system accelerometer_rotation 0; sleep 1; settings get system accelerometer_rotation; settings get system user_rotation\\"", "timeout": 40}\n结果: 0\n0\n\n\nFixed: accelerometer_rotation=0. Screen already cycled Asleep → Awake.\n\nNow report. The user