#M|dsm_20261101171707_682922|assistant|不会因为“被举报用户”就直接删掉私库，但分两条路要说清\n\n**举报账号本身**（判定 spam、滥用、冒充、多号）——平台审的是账号，最重是封号；封号后账号下所有仓库都进不去，私库也在内，但这是封号带来的结果，不是单独“删你的私库”\n\n**举报具体内容**（版权 DMCA、违法内容、恶意代码）——平台可能针对某个仓库发通知并要求下架，私库同样在处理范围内；这种情况才是真的动了仓库，通常是整个仓库被锁或被清空，不会只删其中几个文件\n\n**现实中私库被举报的概率很低**，因为外人根本看不到里面有什么，能触发的只有三种：协作者反手举报、内容泄漏到公开处之后被举报、或者 GitHub 自己的自动扫描命中（恶意软件扫描、密钥扫描这类）\n\n**结论**：正常使用不会因被举报而私库被删，但私库不是保险箱，别往里放明显违规的东西|2026-11-01T17:17:07+08:00||The user is asking whether private repos get deleted if the account is reported. Let me answer accurately.\n\nGitHub's policies: private repositories can be affected by DMCA takedowns (they do process DMCA on private repos, though less commonly), Terms of Service violations, and account suspension affects everything. Reporting an account doesn't automatically delete private repos. But:\n\n- Spam/abuse reports → account review, could suspend account\n- DMCA copyright → GitHub processes takedowns; historically DMCA applies to public repos, but GitHub can act on private repos too, though the DMCA process is about public distribution. Actually GitHub's DMCA process does cover private repos in that they can notify.\n- ToS violations (e.g., hosting malware, illegal content) → can act on private repos\n\nAlso note: content in private repos is much less likely to be reported since nobody can see it. Only the owner, collaborators, or GitHub itself (via malware scanning, secret scanning, etc.) knows.\n\nLet me answer concisely and honestly. The user wants a factual answer. No need for excessive hedging. Keep it reasonably short since the user has repeatedly asked for brevity, though earlier they said "你不用每次都说一句话" — don't say "一句话" every time. So I can answer normally but concise.\n\nAlso per system prompt: no automatic rotation, end with screen off/on... but that's only for tasks. This is a Q&A, no task. Earlier turns in this conversation just answered without the phone rituals when it was pure Q&A. Right — the screen off/on is for task completion. This is a conversation. I'll just answer.\n\nAlso note: no period at end of sentences? "以后不要发送句号" — user asked not to send 句号 (period). Hmm, that's a constraint. I should avoid ending sentences with "。" It's tricky for Chinese text but I can use no punctuation at end of lines, or use other punctuation. Looking at my previous responses, I have been using 。 throughout... Actually let me check the last few responses — I wrote "不会自动被删，除非你三十天没登录..." That ended without 。 Yes. Earlier ones ended without periods too. Let me maintain that: avoid 句号.\n\nLet me write the answer without 句号.\n\nContent:\n\n被举报不会直接导致私库被删，但会走两条不同路径：\n\n1. 举报账号本身（spam、滥用、冒充、多号）→ 平台会审核账号，极端情况封号，封号后所有仓库（含私库）都不可访问，但这是封号导致的结果，不是"删库"\n2. 举报内容（版权 DMCA、违法内容、恶意代码）→ 平台可能针对具体仓库发通知，要求下架或删除，私库也在处理范围内，虽然报的人基本看不到私库内容\n\n关键点：私库内容外人看不到，所以被举报的概率极低，通常只有三种情况会触发\n- 协作者反手举报或泄漏后举报\n- GitHub 自动扫描命中（恶意软件扫描、密钥扫描、CSAM 检测）\n- 你放进去了明显违法的东西且平台被外部要求调查\n\n删减 vs 删除：通常是整个仓库被禁、被锁定、或清空，不会只删其中几个文件\n\n结论：正常使用的私库，被举报删掉的可能很低，但别把它当保险箱\n\nKeep it concise.|{"promptTokens":31972,"promptCacheHitTokens":31744,"promptCacheMissTokens":228,"completionTokens":938,"totalTokens":32910,"apiCalls":1,"reasoningTokens":719}
