6.205.141\nip.klpbbs.com,43.161.202.109\njs-sq-data.klpbbs.com,104.21.76.36\nnb.klpbbs.com,172.67.186.151\nnb-data.klpbbs.com,104.21.76.36\nplayer.klpbbs.com,104.21.76.36\nstatic.klpbbs.com,43.161.202.109\nstatus.klpbbs.com,117.50.76.229\ntc.klpbbs.com,43.161.202.109\nufile.klpbbs.com,103.83.72.202\nuser.klpbbs.com,154.219.105.108\nwj.klpbbs.com,38.76.205.173\nwww.klpbbs.com,38.76.205.155\nzj-data.klpbbs.com,172.67.186.151\nzs-attach.klpbbs.com,104.21.76.36\nzs-data.klpbbs.com,104.21.76.36\n\n\nI got two large data sources. Let me extract unique subdomains. Let me process the crt.sh JSON — it was truncated. I should use a more efficient approach: download and parse with a script. But I don't have the raw file. Let me instead fetch crt.sh with a different output or use a filtering approach.\n\nActually let me just re-request and save to file then parse. Better: use execute_command with curl if available. Let me check environment.\n\nLet me use a script approach: curl crt.sh JSON, extract name_value, dedupe, sort. Then DNS-resolve each to verify live.\n\nLet me check if curl/python3 available.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "which curl python3 dig host 2>/dev/null; echo \\"---\\"; curl -s --max-time 120 \\"https://crt.sh/?q=%25.klpbbs.com&output=json\\" -o /tmp/klp_crt.json; ls -la /tmp/klp_crt.json", "timeout": 150}\n结果: /data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/curl\n/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/python3\n---\nls: cannot access '/tmp/klp_crt.json': No such file or directory\n\n\n/tmp may not exist or is not writable. Termux /tmp might not exist. Use $PREFIX/tmp or $HOME.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd $HOME && curl -s --max-time 150 \\"https://crt.sh/?q=%25.klpbbs.com&output=json\\" -o klp_crt.json; echo \\"rc=$?\\"; ls -la klp_crt.json 2>/dev/null", "timeout": 180}\n结果: rc=0\n-rw-------. 1 u0_a1308 u0_a1308 150 Nov  1 18:48 klp_crt.json\n\n\nOnly 150 bytes — probably rate limited or error. Let me check content.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"co