le. Hmm. But the page text is Japanese. OCR with chi_sim might partially read kanji (kanji are shared with Chinese), so it may read some. Not ideal but something.\n\nLet me first get a screenshot properly:\nadb shell screencap -p /sdcard/Download/shot_tmp.png then that file is in Download already accessible.\n\nLet's do that.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png; sleep 1; ls -l /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png", "timeout": 60}\n结果: * daemon not running; starting now at tcp:5037\n* daemon started successfully\nadb: device '127.0.0.1:5555' not found\n-rw-rw----. 1 root everybody 0 Nov  1 21:10 /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png\n\n\nThe adb connection keeps dropping — likely because each adb invocation restarts the daemon? "daemon not running; starting now" each time means adb server dies between calls. That suggests the adb server process gets killed (phantom process killer / low memory).\n\nBetter approach: run everything in one adb invocation right after adb_up.sh, in a single command chain.\n\nLet me combine: bash adb_up.sh && adb shell screencap.\n\nAlso maybe use `adb connect` manually each time.\n\nLet me do one command: bash adb_up.sh; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png; ls -l ...🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd ~/ddsh && bash adb_up.sh >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png && sleep 1 && ls -l /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png", "timeout": 90}\n结果: 执行失败（退出码 255）\n\nHmm exit 255. The adb server keeps dying. Let me check whether adb_up.sh ends with something that kills adb, or whether the adb daemon is being killed.\n\nLet me run adb_up.sh and immediately adb devices to see.\n\nActually maybe the issue: adb_up.sh connects to 127.0.0.1:5555 but the wireless debugging port rotates? It said "已连接". Then subsequent command fails because server not running—the server restarts and forgets the connection.\n\nSolution: in a single adb invocation chain, start server, connect, then run. Like:\nadb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 && adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell ...\n\nBut if server starts fresh each time, need connect in same command.\n\nLet me try: adb start-server; adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell echo ok\n\nLet me look at adb_up.sh to see what port/how it connects.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cat ~/ddsh/adb_up.sh; echo '---'; pgrep -f adb \p head", "timeout": 30}\n结果: #!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/bash\n# adb_up.sh — 确保 adb 服务在线（开机/掉线后跑一次即可）\nset -u\nD="127.0.0.1:5555"\n\n# 1. 起一个脱离终端的 adb server，避免随 shell 退出而亡\nif ! pgrep -f "adb.*fork-server" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  setsid adb start-server >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &\n  sleep 1.5\nfi\n\n# 2. 连接本机调试端口\nadb connect "$D" >/dev/null 2>&1\nsleep 1\n\n# 3. 校验身份\nUID_LINE=$(adb -s "$D" shell id 2>/dev/null)\nif echo "$UID_LINE" \p grep -q "uid=2000"; then\n  echo "✅ 已连接 $D  ($(echo "$UID_LINE" \p grep -o 'uid=2000(shell)'))"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\necho "❌ 未连上，请确认：设置 → 开发者选项 → 无线调试 已开启"\nexit 1\n---\n19500\n\n\nThe script connects. pgrep shows 19500 for adb. So a server exists. But my adb call said "daemon not running; starting now" — meaning the client couldn't find the server socket, perhaps because ADB_SERVER_SOCKET or HOME differs? Actually the client looks for socket at localhost:5037. Hmm.\n\nWait: after adb_up.sh started the server with setsid, the server lives. Then in a *new* exec_command shell, `adb -s ...` says daemon not running → it starts a new server on 5037, which should connect to existing... unless the old server died.\n\nActually message "daemon not running; starting now at tcp:5037; daemon started successfully" then "device not found" — the new server doesn't have the connection to 127.0.0.1:5555 (adb connect registers with a specific server instance).\n\nSo the fix: each command should do `adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555` in the SAME invocation, since the daemon restarts each time.\n\nLet me combine: adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 && adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell ... all in one command line.\n\nLet's test.\n\nNote: the whole thing must run in one execute_command so the same shell; but each adb client call may restart the daemon... it should stay for the duration. Let's try.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 && adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"wm size; screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png\\" && ls -l /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png", "timeout": 90}\n结果: * daemon not running; starting now at tcp:5037\n* daemon started successfully\nconnected to 127.0.0.1:5555\nPhysical size: 720x1600\n-rw-rw----. 1 root everybody 349448 Nov  1 21:11 /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png\n\n\nScreenshot captured, 349KB. Now let's OCR. Japanese OCR not available (only chi_sim, eng). Japanese kanji may partially read with chi_sim. Let's try chi_sim on it — it will read kanji characters reasonably.\n\nActually better: check what's on screen — maybe browser shows the page. Let me OCR with chi_sim and see.\n\nAlso I can analyze the image programmatically: check colors — the wood cabinet should produce brown pixels, dark background etc. That's a good objective check: presence of brown tones (wood) and light drawer body.\n\nLet me do both: OCR and color statistics.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && tesseract shot_tmp.png ~/ocr_out -l chi_sim 2>/dev/null; echo \\"--- OCR ---\\"; cat ~/ocr_out.txt \p tr -s '\\\\n' '\\\\n' \p head -30", "timeout": 90}\n结果: --- OCR ---\n21:11:07 包                            多 剑四人\p E7)\nGE下\n三“探索未至之境                                +\nclient callmay restart the daemon.… itLshould stay for\nthe duration. Lets tmy\n轩 115j execute_command\n*{command“… 'adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 && adb -\nS 127.0.0.1:5555 shell wm size' screencap\n/storage/emulated/OVDownload/shot tmp.pngV && Is\n-Mstorage/emulateq/O/Downlioad/shot tmp.png'，\n:imeout 90)}\n从L忆未口未L盛。引考出L式 (下口口一) 0\nHTML在作成由未才。未茸adb shell橙限在取得\nL、环境在确认未才。adb shell椎限在取得\n未L励。回轻设定志确认L2?2了>?、HTML在作成\n未才。环境确认完了 (回园=0下才了、画面\n720x1600) 。引雯出L式UIOHTML碟作成由未\n才。了了熙儿在作成未上万。构造D受当性志\n检证L 未才。构造柳证OK (未于镇名今太L、4\n2OD引考出L) 。窒际O了三客示下描画确认上L\n发消息或按住说话\nKTCICGOICICIGT .\n和 Q\n 罩\n\n\nThe screenshot shows the harness chat page (DeepSeek), not the browser. So the file:// intent didn't actually open a browser, or it opened and then we switched back? Actually the am start command was in a previous shell where adb connection failed ("device not found"), so it never actually started. Then later "am start" was run in a successful connection? Let me re-check: the am start command returned "Starting: Intent {...}" — that was successful (with the connection that worked). Hmm, that was the second attempt after adb_up.sh. It said "Starting: Intent ..." which means it was dispatched. But maybe the file:// URL isn't handled by browser (file access restrictions), so nothing opened, and screen remained the harness.\n\nWait, but the chat page shows my command echoed — the screen is the harness app.\n\nSo I need to open the HTML properly. Options:\n1. Use a browser app with package launch: e.g., com.heytap.browser (OPPO browser) with intent.\n2. Use Chrome-based intent.\n\nfile:// scheme may be blocked. Alternative: serve via local HTTP server (python3 -m http.server) and open http://127.0.0.1:8080/drawer_ui.html.\n\nThat's more reliable. Let me start a tiny http server in background in Download dir, then am start VIEW http://127.0.0.1:8080/drawer_ui.html.\n\nLet's do it in one command chain: start server in background, wait, adb connect, am start, sleep, screencap.\n\nNote: server must persist between commands — use nohup/setsid.\n\nLet me do:\ncd /storage/emulated/0/Download && setsid python3 -m http.server 8899 >/dev/null 2>&1 &\nsleep 2\ncurl check\nadb connect; am start -a VIEW -d http://127.0.0.1:8899/drawer_ui.html\nsleep 4; screencap\n\nThen screenshot, OCR.\n\nLet me be careful about which browser handles it. am start VIEW http URL should open default browser.\n\nLet's go.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && (setsid python3 -m http.server 8899 >/dev/null 2>&1 &) ; sleep 2; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \\"http:%{http_code}\\\\n\\" http://127.0.0.1:8899/drawer_ui.html", "timeout": 60}\n结果: http:200\n\n\nHTTP server works. Now open in browser via adb.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d 'http://127.0.0.1:8899/drawer_ui.html'\\" 2>&1 \p head -4; sleep 6; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png; ls -l /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png", "timeout": 120}\n结果: Starting: Intent { act=android.intent.action.VIEW dat=http://127.0.0.1:8899/... }\n-rw-rw----. 1 root everybody 365529 Nov  1 21:11 /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png\n\n\n🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nim = Image.open('shot_tmp.png').convert('RGB')\\nw,h = im.size\\nprint('size', w, h)\\npx = im.load()\\n# サンプリング統計\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nc = Counter()\\nbrown = 0; dark = 0; light = 0; tot = 0\\nfor y in range(0, h, 6):\\n    for x in range(0, w, 6):\\n        r,g,b = px[x,y]; tot += 1\\n        c[(r//32,g//32,b//32)] += 1\\n        if r>g>b and r-b>25 and r>50: brown += 1\\n        elif (r+g+b)/3 < 45: dark += 1\\n        elif (r+g+b)/3 > 170: light += 1\\nprint('brown%%=%.1f dark%%=%.1f light%%=%.1f' % (brown*100/tot, dark*100/tot, light*100/tot))\\nprint('top colors:')\\nfor k,v in c.most_common(6):\\n    print('  rgb~', tuple(i*32+16 for i in k), '%.1f%%' % (v*100/tot))\\nPY", "timeout": 60}\n结果: size 720 1600\nbrown%=22.2 dark%=47.6 light%=25.1\ntop colors:\n  rgb~ (240, 240, 240) 17.4%\n  rgb~ (16, 16, 16) 15.4%\n  rgb~ (80, 48, 48) 14.8%\n  rgb~ (16, 16, 48) 12.0%\n  rgb~ (48, 48, 16) 8.0%\n  rgb~ (16, 48, 48) 6.2%\n\n\nInteresting: there's 22% brown, 25% light. Hmm, but this could still be the chat page? The chat page is dark with some colors. Let me OCR to see.\n\nActually rgb~(240,240,240) 17.4% = white/light area, rgb~(80,48,48) 14.8% is brownish. Could be our page. But let's OCR.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && tesseract shot_tmp.png ~/ocr2 -l chi_sim 2>/dev/null; head -35 ~/ocr2.txt \p grep -v '^\\\\s*$'", "timeout": 90}\n结果: 21:11:26 包                   媒人念四名\nO、 加 引出L 1 Draw， 立   白\n引志出LUI          六\n引走出L式咎之名一了了工一又\n木岗寺闻已订闵上                 4段\n书上类\n”DOCUMENTS                “人\n契约书' 保证书， 领尿书O三点七义卜。年度\n忆之们封简下仁切2忆矶口未下。\n2026 年度     要返却     原本\n下居\nTooLS\n食一7几\nCABLES\n和 QQ =三   四\n\n\nThe page is rendering. OCR reads "引出L 1 Draw" (引き出し UI Drawer), "引走出L式咎之名一了了工一又" (引き出し式インターフェース), "木岗寺闻已订闵上 4段" (木製キャビネット 4段), "书上类 DOCUMENTS" (書類), "契约书' 保证书， 领尿书O三点七义卜" = 契約書・保証書・領収書の三点セット, "2026 年度 要返却 原本" chips, "下居 TOOLS" (工具), "CABLES", etc.\n\nSo it renders, and the first drawer is auto-opened showing content. \n\nOCR with chi_sim reads Japanese poorly but content is confirmed present. The wood cabinet, chips (2026年度/要返却/原本), sections 書類/工具/ケーブル all visible.\n\nLet me also verify the side drawers work — tap the hamburger and screenshot. That requires input tap via adb. Hamberger button is at top-left roughly x≈36, y≈? The topbar starts at top with safe area. Screen 720x1600. topbar padding 13px, button 42px → center y ≈ 13+21 = 34 (CSS px) but device pixel ratio? Viewport meta width=device-width, so CSS px = device px / dpr. Screenshot 720x1600 is physical pixels. If dpr is 2, then CSS 360x800. Button center CSS (15+21, 13+21) = (36, 34) → physical (72, 68).\n\nHmm. Let me check dpr by reading window.devicePixelRatio — can't easily. Instead, just tap at physical (72,68) and see.\n\nActually let me verify the drawer opens by tapping hamburger, screenshot, and check that the left panel appears (nav items like ホーム/引き出し一覧).\n\nLet me do: adb input tap 72 68, sleep 1, screencap, OCR.\n\nBut careful: we must not disturb. It's fine.\n\nAlso note the toast for the page. Let's test.\n\nLet me run.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"input tap 72 68\\"; sleep 2; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png; cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && tesseract shot_tmp.png ~/ocr3 -l chi_sim 2>/dev/null; grep -v '^\\\\s*$' ~/ocr3.txt \p head -20", "timeout": 120}\n结果: 21:11:40                   偶合\n交\n画面四配色在切口蔡元\n操作音在吃与才\n12并《之他顾开总吾\n开W忆w\\吾引走出由在必才\n祥一夕示一叉代放L 让\nL无\n吕I\p ED)\n名\n中国卓。\n\n\nIt opened the right drawer? The OCR shows "画面四配色在切口蔡元" (画面の配色を切り替え), "操作音在吃与才" (操作音を鳴らす), "12并《之他顾开总吾" (1つ開くと他を閉じる), "開いている引き出しを戻す" (開いている引き出しを戻す), "すべて閉じる" (祥一夕示一又代放L 让 → すべて閉じる).\n\nSo it opened the RIGHT drawer (settings) — because my tap at x=72 might have hit the right button? No... Right button is at top-right (x≈648 physical if 720 wide). Hmm, but OCR shows settings panel content.\n\nWait — maybe tap x=72,y=68 hit... Actually maybe dpr makes CSS width 360, so topbar right button at CSS x≈345 → physical 690. My tap at 72 physical = CSS 36 → left button. Hmm.\n\nBut the OCR content is clearly settings (配色/操作音/1つ開くと他を閉じる/すべて閉じる). So the right drawer opened. Unless... the left drawer content also would show メニュー/ホーム/引き出し一覧.\n\nSo tap opened right drawer unexpectedly? Odd. Maybe my earlier tap at (72,68) actually fell on... hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the panel is showing because after opening left drawer, the screenshot captured... no.\n\nAlternatively the tap hit the backdrop of previously opened drawer? No.\n\nLet me look at OCR more: "偶合 交" at top, "中国卓。" bottom - that's the chat input artifact? Actually "中国卓。" might be leftover.\n\nHmm, hard to tell. It's possible my tap hit the gear at right because CSS layout: if dpr=1.0 then CSS width=720 and right button at x≈690-702, not 72.\n\nConfusing. But regardless — one of the drawers opened and displays the settings switches, which proves the drawer mechanism works.\n\nLet me take a fresh screenshot with a different approach: get the current screen and check panel position via pixel analysis — is the panel anchored left or right? I can check column brightness: if the panel is on the left side, left columns are lighter (panel bg #161b24=22,27,36) vs backdrop dark overlay. Hmm both dark.\n\nBetter: let me use dumpsys/uiautomator to dump UI hierarchy and find the text — but it's a WebView, so accessibility nodes may expose text. Let me try `uiautomator dump` and grep.\n\nActually simpler: verify both drawers by tapping precisely based on measured positions from UI dump. Let me dump UI to see the actual node bounds for the buttons — WebView often exposes accessibility nodes with bounds.\n\nLet me try: adb shell uiautomator dump /sdcard/Download/ui.xml then grep.\n\nThat gives real coordinates. Good idea — that's proper verification.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"uiautomator dump /storage/emulated/0/Download/ui_tmp.xml\\" 2>&1 \p tail -2; cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport re\\ns=open('ui_tmp.xml',encoding='utf-8').read()\\nprint('len',len(s))\\nfor m in re.finditer(r'text=\\"([^\\"]+)\\"[^>]*bounds=\\"(\\\\[[^\\"]+\\\\])\\"', s):\\n    t,b=m.group(1),m.group(2)\\n    if t.strip(): print(repr(t), b)\\nPY", "timeout": 120}\n结果: UI hierchary dumped to: /storage/emulated/0/Download/ui_tmp.xml\nlen 9127\n'搜狗输入法' [312,99][452,137]\n'中文' [225,167][325,205]\n'英文' [395,167][459,205]\n'玩命加载中' [290,475][430,525]\n\n\nThe screen is showing the Sogou input method panel ("搜狗输入法", "中文", "英文") — meaning the browser page lost focus / keyboard opened. "玩命加载中" = loading. Hmm, so the browser didn't render? Wait, it says 玩命加载中 which means "loading desperately" — that's from the browser page (maybe a loading state).\n\nHmm, so what happened: my tap at (72,68) maybe tapped into... Actually the UI dump shows Sogou keyboard, meaning a text field got focus. That's weird for our page (no inputs).\n\nPerhaps the previous am start didn't open a browser but rather our page is in some other context... Or the tap closed the drawer and hit something else.\n\nWait, "玩命加载中" could be the DeepSeek harness page loading. So maybe the harness page came back to front and keyboard opened.\n\nThe screenshots earlier had the page rendering though (OCR read 引き出し UI, 木製キャビネット). So the browser did display the page. Then something switched.\n\nLet me be systematic:\n1. Check current foreground app.\n2. Force stop the harness? No — we shouldn't disrupt user's app. Actually opening browser is fine but I shouldn't kill things unnecessarily.\n\nLet me check current app and then re-open the page and immediately screenshot.\n\nPlan: \n- am start VIEW http://127.0.0.1:8899/drawer_ui.html\n- sleep 5\n- screencap\n- OCR to confirm page\nThen tap hamburger using coordinates derived from CSS with known dpr. To know dpr, I can add a JS-display? Can't. But I can compute from rendering: the hero card max-width 720px CSS and main padding 15px; the cabinet occupies most of width. Alternatively, get dpr via `adb shell dumpsys window \p grep density` or `wm density`.\n\nLet me get wm density: physical 720x1600, density maybe 320 (dpr 2.0) → CSS 360x800.\n\nIf dpr = physical_width / CSS_width. Let me check `adb shell wm density`.\n\nThen compute button center in CSS: left button: topbar padding 13px top, 15px left; button 42px → center CSS (15+21, 13+21)=(36,34) → physical = (36*dpr, 34*dpr + statusbar?). The page is drawn from top of window; status bar is separate (WebView content starts below status bar if not fullscreen). The topbar is sticky at top of viewport. Viewport top = below status bar (~24-30 CSS px). Hmm, so physical y offset includes status bar height.\n\nInstead of guessing, I can compute from the screenshot: find the hamburger button visually. Or simply add a temporary test: use JS? Can't inject.\n\nAlternative approach to verify drawers: skip tap-based and instead just verify rendering + hit-testing indirectly. But the user wants a working drawer; verifying interaction is valuable.\n\nBetter: I can make the page auto-open drawers for a moment? That's hacky.\n\nAlternative: use OCR-derived positions. From the earlier screenshot OCR I could locate text like "引志出LUI" (title) position. tesseract TSV gives bounding boxes. Then hamburger is left of title, vertically aligned with title center.\n\nLet me do that: OCR the screenshot with TSV, find "Draw" or "UI" box → its y center = topbar center; then hamburger x ≈ (title_left - 50).\n\nLet's do that programmatically.\n\nSteps:\n1. adb connect; am start; sleep 5; screencap\n2. python: OCR tsv, find text containing 'UI' or 'Draw' or '引出'\n3. compute tap point, tap, screencap, OCR to check for メニュー items.\n\nLet me first re-open page and capture, then compute.\n\nAlso kill the Sogou keyboard: press back/escape to dismiss. Let me send `input keyevent 4` (BACK) after am start? That may navigate back in browser. Let's just am start fresh (it will bring browser to front) and then take screenshot.\n\nLet me proceed.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"input keyevent 111; wm density; dumpsys window 2>/dev/null \p grep -m1 -E 'mCurrentFocus\pmFocusedApp'\\" 2>&1 \p head -6; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d 'http://127.0.0.1:8899/drawer_ui.html'\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; sleep 5; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell screencap -p /storage/emulated/0/Download/shot_tmp.png; cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && tesseract shot_tmp.png ~/ocr4 tsv 2>/dev/null; python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport csv\\nrows=[r for r in csv.DictReader(open('/data/data/com.termux/files/home/ocr4.tsv'),