ation: DONE (screenshot at 21:11:26 read our content).\n\nNow interaction verification: the tap at (72,68) produced a screenshot whose OCR showed settings items (配色/操作音/1つ開くと他を閉じる/すべて閉じる). That's the RIGHT drawer (設定). So a drawer opened via tap — but which button? At x=72 physical = CSS 36 → that's the left button. Hmm, but content was settings...\n\nUnless... the left drawer's nav list also includes 設定 item, but not 操作音/ライトテーマ.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the screenshot I OCR'd at 21:11:40 was of the right drawer because my tap landed on the gear. If dpr=2, left button CSS center (36,34+statusbar). Physical x = 72. So x=72 → left button. Unless the browser page has horizontal offset...\n\nActually hold on: y=68 physical = CSS 34. The viewport starts below the status bar (status bar ~ 25-30 CSS px?). CSS 34 within viewport = topbar area, fine.\n\nMaybe the tap opened the left drawer, and then... no, OCR clearly showed 操作音/配色.\n\nPossibly the tap missed the button and hit the backdrop? No backdrop then.\n\nAlternatively, my tap at (72,68) might have hit the LEFT button, opening the left drawer; then the screenshot at 21:11:40 — the OCR text "画面四配色在切口蔡元" might actually be part of the visible page content? No, the page doesn't have that text except in the right drawer.\n\nHmm, wait: the hint text at the bottom says "取っ手をタップで開閉 ・ 外側をタップでサイドドロワーが閉じます ・ 設定で「すべて閉じる」も使えます". Not matching.\n\nSo the right drawer was open. Possibly because my tap at y=68 hit... hmm, if the page is scrolled? No.\n\nWhatever — the important thing: a drawer opens on tap. Let me verify each drawer deliberately:\n\nLeft button physical center: CSS (36, 13+21=34) + viewport top offset. Viewport top = status bar height. In heytap browser, the page may be inside a window with its own top offset (browser UI). Actually the browser has no toolbar if opened via intent? Earlier screenshot showed browser with content and a bottom tab bar (icons at y 1475). So there IS browser chrome: bottom bar ~ y>1440, and maybe a top address bar.\n\nIf browser has a top toolbar of e.g. 50 CSS px, then our topbar is shifted down.\n\nGiven uncertainty, best approach: find the hamburger by detecting it from the screenshot. The topbar contains: hamburger (rounded square with 3 lines), title "引き出し UI", gear button at right.\n\nFrom OCR tsv at 21:11:26 (our page), text 'O、 加 引出L 1 Draw， 立   白' — that line is the topbar title. I can get its box. Let me instead directly locate the two buttons by pixel analysis: look for the icon-btn rounded rects — they are lighter (#1d2431→#161b24) on darker bg. Meh.\n\nSimplest robust path: use the browser's own accessibility tree via uiautomator — WebView exposes nodes but earlier dump showed only Sogou. Let me dump again now that browser is focused; the page's accessibility nodes may appear with text like "引き出し UI" and clickable buttons with bounds. That would give exact coordinates.\n\nLet me try the dump again.🔧 调用工具: execute_command\n参数: {"command": "adb connect 127.0.0.1:5555 >/dev/null 2>&1; adb -s 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \\"uiautomator dump /storage/emulated/0/Download/ui_tmp.xml\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; cd /storage/emulated/0/Download && python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport re\\ns=open('ui_tmp.xml',encoding='utf-8').read()\\nprint('len',len(s))\\nnodes=re.findall(r'<node[^>]*>', s)\\nprint('nodes',len(nodes))\\nfor n in nodes:\\n    t=re.search(r'text=\\"([^\\"]*)\\"',n); d=re.search(r'content-desc=\\"([^\\"]*)\\"',n)\\n    b=re.search(r'bounds=\\"(\\\\[[^\\"]+\\\\])\\"',n); c=re.search(r'class=\\"([^\\"]*)\\"',n)\\n    tv=(t.group(1) if t else '') or (d.group(1) if d else '')\\n    if tv.strip(): print(repr(tv[:40]), c.group(1).split('.')[-1] if c else '', b.group(1) if b else '')\\nPY", "timeout": 120}\n结果: len 27550\nnodes 85\n'好的&#10;敬语' TextView [598,0][660,5]\n'かしこまりました。' TextView [95,70][333,123]\n'劳驾您帮我写个html代码，html代码就是一个抽屉样式的代码，然后保存到我的下' TextView [165,188][660,384]\n'お手数をおかけいたしますが、引き出し-styleのHTMLコードを作成していただ' TextView [45,449][679,661]\n'复制' View [49,696][87,734]\n'喜欢' View [125,696][163,734]\n'不喜欢' View [201,696][239,734]\n'朗读' Button [251,670][327,760]\n'分享' View [353,696][391,734]\n'重新生成' View [637,696][675,734]\n'打开侧边栏' View [27,90][72,135]\n'日语敬语翻译请求' TextView [114,93][354,132]\n'自动朗读' View [532,68][622,158]\n'开启新对话' View [652,90][697,135]\n'回答由 AI 生成，仅供参考' TextView [0,0][0,0]\n'劳驾您再把其里面的内容全部翻译成中文&#10;' EditText [53,831][663,920]\n'深度思考' TextView [107,971][211,1005]\n'智能搜索' TextView [310,971][414,1005]\n'上传文件' View [533,964][580,1013]\n'发送' View [625,973][655,1003]\n\n\nNow it's clear: the foreground is the DeepSeek Harness app (not the browser) — this is the chat UI. So the browser came and went. The mCurrentFocus earlier said com.heytap.browser, but now the dump shows the harness chat.\n\nWait — the harness chat might BE running inside the browser (DeepSeek Harness is a web app? Actually "Harness" app). Hmm, class names like "打开侧边栏" (mainDrawer) suggest Compose/Flutter UI.\n\nAnyway: currently the harness is front. Which means my "am start VIEW http URL" opened the browser briefly, and then something returned to the harness — possibly my `input keyevent 111` (ESC) closed the browser, and then subsequent am start went to browser... \n\nHmm, but the dump right now shows harness. So the last am start might have failed (browser opened but then... ).\n\nReality check: earlier screenshots DID show our page (OCR at 21:11:26 gave 引き出し UI, 木製キャビネット). That is genuine proof the HTML renders correctly in the browser. Good.\n\nBut then the browser was pushed to background — perhaps because of my repeated adb shell commands? Unlikely. More likely: the OPPO browser has aggressive background killing, OR the harness app was brought back by something.\n\nAnyway, current state: harness is foreground, user sees chat.\n\nFor verification of drawer interactions, opening the browser each time is fragile. Let me think about whether interaction verification is essential. I've verified:\n- HTML valid structure\n- Renders in real browser (OCR e